      "id": "S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT",
      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7B ('Licence attribution: CC-BY entries show their attribution in the Library and Materials windows and in the Details view, and kits carry it in their snapshots'; 'Export: any entry \u2192 its -json file; a selection or a category \u2192 a catalogue folder. Exporting pins the exported versions (\u00a7C)'), \u00a7A ('Catalogue folder layout': uniqueness per kind within a catalogue is checked on export), \u00a7C ('A version becomes Pinned \u2014 a one-way flag \u2014 when a kit first references it, or when it is exported'; '\"Export my library\" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder, which the recreated database imports'), \u00a7G ('Exports'); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 14 (S3.3) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a74, \u00a75, \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a710",
      "requirement": "Step 120: The Library window exports the selected entry, the shown entries and the user's whole library, and credits the licensed materials of a selected sample (001 \u00a7B 'Export', 'Licence attribution'; 001 \u00a7C '\"Export my library\" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder'; .spec-md \u00a710.1: 'Export my library\u2026' is in the Library window; the S3.3 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowError` gains `LibraryExportRefusedErr of LibraryExportError`, documented, and its `caption` renders it through `LibraryExportError.caption` (step 119). (b) `LibraryWindowModel` gains `entryExportStatus : ControlCaption option`, `None` when the window opens, with a one-line doc. (c) `member this.exportableSelection : LibraryEntryEnvelope option` is, in Browse mode, the selected entry's latest envelope through `entry.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId` (step 24) and `context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope` (step 116), and `None` otherwise, as step 119's is. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry of FileName`, `ExportShownLibraryEntries of CatalogueExportTarget` and `ExportMyLibrary of CatalogueExportTarget`. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry file` is inert without an `exportableSelection`, and otherwise calls `context.catalogueImports.exportEntry` of its id and `file`. `ExportShownLibraryEntries target` calls `exportEntries` over the ids of `m.filteredEntries` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:518`), each `e.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId`. `ExportMyLibrary target` calls `exportUserLibrary target` (step 117). `Ok` sets `entryExportStatus` to the outcome's `exportedCaption` (step 119) and clears `lastError`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `Some (LibraryExportRefusedErr e)` and clears `entryExportStatus`. None of them arms or disarms a gate, or changes the selection or the mode. (f) The view. In the verbs row (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1104`), in Browse mode and after 