      "requirement": "Step 135: An experiment's data file becomes a kit attachment, read through the kit by its relative path (001 \u00a7E 'References inside a kit are relative paths \u2026', 'Absolute paths are never stored'; the S4.2 brief: `Experiments.DataFilePath`, an absolute path string today, is replaced by `DataAttachment` in `Experiment.dataFileOpt` and `attachDataFile`; `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` and `ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate` read through the kit by relative path; no kit file stores an absolute path). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once. (1) Domain. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs` opens `Kit`. `DataFilePath` (`Experiments.fs:DataFilePath`) is deleted. `Experiment.dataFileOpt` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) becomes `DataAttachment option` (step 132), and `attachDataFile` (`Experiments.fs:attachDataFile`) takes `(attachment : DataAttachment)`. Their docs say the attachment is a kit-relative path and its hash (spec 0050 S4.2). (b) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs`, after `DataFileText` (`MeasuredData.fs:DataFileText`): `type Kit.KitFileText with member this.dataFileText : DataFileText` hands a kit file's text to the measured-data parsers, in one direction only (ELEV006). Its doc is one line. (c) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs`: `ExperimentDataProxy` (`ExperimentDataProxy.fs:ExperimentDataProxy`) opens `Kit` and becomes `{ attachDataFile : FileName -> Result<DataAttachment, KitError>; attachmentStatus : DataAttachment -> Result<DataAttachmentStatus, KitError>; tryLoadIntensity : DataAttachment -> Result<IntensitySeries, ExperimentDataError>; tryLoadEllipsometric : DataAttachment -> Result<EllipsometricSeries, ExperimentDataError> }`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`. Each field has a one-line doc: attach a picked file to the kit, in place inside it and copied into `data/` otherwise; the attachment's status now; and the two loads by the attachment's kit p