      "requirement": "Step 144: The kit's resolution rows go to the one import dialog (001 \u00a7E 'One dialog shows all rows; nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; .spec-md \u00a710.1 'The import dialog opens \u2026 on a kit whose snapshot needs decisions', \u00a710.3 identify \u2192 confirm, \u00a710.5 the Apply / Cancel pair; step 107: 'S4.2 adds a kit snapshot's case'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs` (step 107): `ImportDialogRequest` gains `ResolveKitSnapshot of kit : KitLibraryContext * decisions : ImportDecision list`, documented as a kit's snapshot rows (step 141). `decisions` answers its rows. `heading` is `Open kit <kit name>: <k> library entries need a decision.`, `k` counting every snapshot row, including `SameContentHash`. `ImportDialogApplied.summary` is `Opened the library of kit <kit name> (decisions applied: <n>).`. For this case, `ApplyImportChoices` calls `kit.confirm m.choices` (step 143), and its `Ok` and `Error` are handled as the other cases' are, so `onApplied` receives the outcome, whose re-bindings the opener overlays (step 142). Every other message, the rows, the diff preview and the Apply / Cancel row are unchanged, and Cancel applies nothing. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, `ImportDecision.actionCaption` (step 107): under `KitSnapshotOrigin` (step 140), `SkipIncomingEntry` reads `Keep the kit's copy (read-only)`; `AddIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library`, or `Add to my library, side by side` on a `NameCollision`; `AddIncomingVersion _` reads `Add this version to my library`; and `ForkIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library as a fork`. Every other action, and every action under another origin, keeps its caption. The dialog opens for a kit wherever the app opens one, and this step adds no window, id or message. (3) Tests, in `ImportDialogTests` (step 107). Each runs over a kit snapshotted (step 139) from `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` with the multilayer sample's references, then opened