      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7I ('Kit.Item = one PHYSICAL piece: ItemId (GUID) and an ItemLabel; the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted); its own Parameter values; optional photo (a kit file) and notes'; 'ItemModel \u2014 parameterised physics, a library entry (.item-model-json). Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated'; the model table; 'Parameter = a name plus a ParameterState: Known | Unknown of start * bounds * prior option | Calibrated of value * sigma * fromFitRun'; 'Dial mapping'; 'Revisions'; 'Material parameters as unknowns'), \u00a7A (library and kit extensions, the kit's flat root, module Kit), \u00a7B (entry files, schemas, the shipped catalogue, import), \u00a7C (the library proxies gain a SQLite create; contract tests; pinning), \u00a7E (library closure snapshot), \u00a7N, \u00a7P (AddItem, SetParameterState; KitProxy; every proxy has an in-memory stub), \u00a7Q (the bench noise model's types); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 23 (S7.1) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.3, \u00a73.11, \u00a73.14, \u00a73.17, \u00a73.23, \u00a74, \u00a75 (Kit module, ItemModel), \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79; 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6 require complete item mapping before S7; shared prerequisites are scheduled in S6.",
      "requirement": "Step 205: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. One home for the parameter vocabulary that items, item models and the fitter share, compiled early enough for the library entries and the kit (the S7.1 brief: a Parameter's name REUSES `MuellerInverse.ParameterName` and a dial's sign REUSES `MuellerReconstruction.DialSign`; .spec-md \u00a74: a reuse is a move). `MuellerInverse.fs` and `MuellerReconstruction.fs` compile last in Domain, after `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (step 24) and `Kit.fs` (step 122), which must name both types, so both MOVE. This step changes no behaviour. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`: `module ItemModels` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ElementId.fs` and before `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (one `<Compile Include=\"ItemModels.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment). Its module doc is one to three lines: the parameter vocabulary of items and item models (spec 0050 S7.1). (2) `ParameterName` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ParameterName`, the single-case union over `string` with `.value`) moves into it unchanged; its doc keeps its text and adds that spec 0050 S7.1 moved it here. `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels` and declares it no more, so `ParameterAxis.name` and every axis list read the moved type. (3) `DialSign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:DialSign`: `DialPositive` | `DialNegative` with `member this.value : float`, +1 / \u22121) moves after it unchanged, its doc likewise. `MuellerReconstruction.fs` opens `ItemModels`, and `AnalyzerModel.dialSign` and `physicalAngle` read it as today. (4) The consumers open the module where the compiler asks and change nothing else: `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/DesignParameters.fs`; and in `Berreman/BerremanTests/` `InverseFitHarness.fs`, `MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `OptimizationTests.fs` and `MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`. No alias, re-export or second declaration remains (ELEV014), so `git grep -n -E \"type (ParameterName|DialSign) =\" -- Berreman/` finds only `ItemModels.fs`. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs`, `module ItemModelsTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels`. `the moved parameter name and dial sign keep their values`: `(ParameterName \"c2.retardance\").value` is `c2.retardance`, `DialPositive.value` is 1.0 and `DialNegative.value` is \u22121.0. No BerremanTests fact changes. `OptimizationTests` (whose fixture builds `ParameterName` values) and `MuellerReconstructionTests` (whose analyzer models carry `DialPositive` and `DialNegative`) are the cheapest BerremanTests classes that exercise the two types, and they run unchanged. Acceptance: After the move, `ParameterName` and `DialSign` MUST be declared only in `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`, compiled before `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`; unit-tests MUST pass over `OptimizationTests` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` with their numbers unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the moved parameter name and dial sign keep their values`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
