      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7I ('Kit.Item = one PHYSICAL piece: ItemId (GUID) and an ItemLabel; the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted); its own Parameter values; optional photo (a kit file) and notes'; 'ItemModel \u2014 parameterised physics, a library entry (.item-model-json). Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated'; the model table; 'Parameter = a name plus a ParameterState: Known | Unknown of start * bounds * prior option | Calibrated of value * sigma * fromFitRun'; 'Dial mapping'; 'Revisions'; 'Material parameters as unknowns'), \u00a7A (library and kit extensions, the kit's flat root, module Kit), \u00a7B (entry files, schemas, the shipped catalogue, import), \u00a7C (the library proxies gain a SQLite create; contract tests; pinning), \u00a7E (library closure snapshot), \u00a7N, \u00a7P (AddItem, SetParameterState; KitProxy; every proxy has an in-memory stub), \u00a7Q (the bench noise model's types); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 23 (S7.1) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.3, \u00a73.11, \u00a73.14, \u00a73.17, \u00a73.23, \u00a74, \u00a75 (Kit module, ItemModel), \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79; 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6 require complete item mapping before S7; shared prerequisites are scheduled in S6.",
      "requirement": "Step 206: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Define the detector noise data required by 001 \u00a7I without moving the bench implementation before 001 \u00a7Q / \u00a7S10. In OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs, after ParameterName and DialSign from step 205: `ParameterValue of double` with `.value`, one parameter's number in its kind's unit. `ParameterKind` = `AngleParameter` (radians: an azimuth, an axis or dial offset, an ellipticity angle, a rotation uncertainty) | `PhaseParameter` (radians: a retardance) | `FractionParameter` (dimensionless in [0, 1]: an extinction ratio, a diattenuation, a degree of polarization, an element or throughput uncertainty) | `ScaleParameter` (a dimensionless multiplier: an intensity scale, a gain) | `MuellerElementParameter` (one Mueller-matrix element) | `ThicknessParameter` (metres) | `ReadingParameter` (a detector reading in its own units: a dark offset). `ItemParameterAxis = { name : ParameterName; kind : ParameterKind; defaultValue : ParameterValue }` is one parameter a model publishes. Detector model files store their axis descriptors, so ParameterKind MUST carry stable integer wire tags 1 through 7 in the declaration order above and tryOfWire : int -> ParameterKind option, with zero and unrecognized tags returning None. Its text rendering MUST remain separate from its tag. On ItemParameterAxis, declare static member detectorNoiseAxes (rotation : ParameterValue) (element : ParameterValue) (throughput : ParameterValue) : ItemParameterAxis list. It MUST return rotationUncertainty with AngleParameter, then elementUncertainty and throughputUncertainty with FractionParameter, preserving the supplied values. A detector model MUST carry that ItemParameterAxis list; an instantiated item carries the corresponding ordinary Parameter states. Domain MUST NOT declare or reference AngleUncertainty, ElementUncertainty, ThroughputUncertainty or NoiseParam. Their sole declarations MUST remain in Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs until step 339 moves all four to Optimization/BenchNoise.fs. No new noise-budget record, duplicated bench constants, dependency from Domain to Optimization, or product reference to a test assembly is permitted. In ItemModelsTests, add `the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities`: construct elevated test-local rotation, element and throughput values (0.001 radians, 0.02 and 0.03), call detectorNoiseAxes, and assert names, kinds, order and exact defaults. This data-projection test MUST NOT claim to test a promoted bench model. The axis fact MUST verify every ParameterKind tag round-trips and that zero and an unrecognized tag return None. Acceptance: After detector noise axes are defined, Domain MUST publish the three named axes with the supplied values, without declaring any bench-noise type; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass including `the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities`, the count rising by 1; build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
