      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7I ('Kit.Item = one PHYSICAL piece: ItemId (GUID) and an ItemLabel; the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted); its own Parameter values; optional photo (a kit file) and notes'; 'ItemModel \u2014 parameterised physics, a library entry (.item-model-json). Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated'; the model table; 'Parameter = a name plus a ParameterState: Known | Unknown of start * bounds * prior option | Calibrated of value * sigma * fromFitRun'; 'Dial mapping'; 'Revisions'; 'Material parameters as unknowns'), \u00a7A (library and kit extensions, the kit's flat root, module Kit), \u00a7B (entry files, schemas, the shipped catalogue, import), \u00a7C (the library proxies gain a SQLite create; contract tests; pinning), \u00a7E (library closure snapshot), \u00a7N, \u00a7P (AddItem, SetParameterState; KitProxy; every proxy has an in-memory stub), \u00a7Q (the bench noise model's types); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 23 (S7.1) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.3, \u00a73.11, \u00a73.14, \u00a73.17, \u00a73.23, \u00a74, \u00a75 (Kit module, ItemModel), \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79; 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6 require complete item mapping before S7; shared prerequisites are scheduled in S6.",
      "requirement": "Step 207: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. What a parameter is, and the parameters the existing models publish (001 \u00a7I: 'Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated, not hand-written'; the S7.1 brief: names, kinds, defaults, an item's parameters created from them; .spec-md \u00a73.14: the source preset, the ideal LP / CP presets and the stack `Sample` are models themselves). In `ItemModels.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `Berreman.Media` (`Thickness`), `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Library`. Using step 206's ParameterValue, ParameterKind and ItemParameterAxis, add the three physics type extensions, each member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list. (a) On `SourcePreset` (`ElementId.fs:SourcePreset`), the light source over the preset's \u03bb (001 \u00a7I 'Light source | \u03bb or tunable limits (exists) + output polarization (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization) + an intensity scale'): `azimuth` and `ellipticity` (`AngleParameter`, 0), `degreeOfPolarization` (`FractionParameter`, 0) and `intensityScale` (`ScaleParameter`, 1), so the default is unpolarized light at unit scale (001 \u00a7N). \u03bb and the tunable limits stay the preset's, as today. (b) On `PolarizerPreset` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`): `[]`, because an ideal LP or CP, or a constant-Mueller compound, has no parameter (001 \u00a7I 'Ideal LP / ideal CP | None'). (c) On `Sample` (`ElementId.fs:Sample`): one `ThicknessParameter` per layer of finite thickness, in stack order, defaulting to that thickness in metres. A `SingleLayer` at film position k (1-based) is `film<k>.thickness`; layer j of a `Repeated` group at position k is `film<k>.layer<j>.thickness`, shared by every period; the substrate plate is `substrate.thickness`; a layer of `Thickness.Infinity` publishes nothing. `type Thickness with member this.parameterValueOpt : ParameterValue option` (`Infinity` is `None`) is the one conversion. A sample's materials publish nothing here: a study opens a material version and owns its unknowns (001 \u00a7I 'Material parameters as unknowns'; S11.1). No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests` (step 206), each comparing axis lists with `=`: `a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633).parameterAxes` is exactly the four axes above. `an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter`: the polarizer of `BuiltinCatalogue.preset PresetIds.polarizerLp` publishes `[]`. `a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId).parameterAxes` is one `substrate.thickness` axis at 1e-3 and `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id`'s one `film1.thickness` axis at 6e-7 (each value within 1e-15); a test-local structure of one 5 nm layer and a `Repeated` group over a 10 nm and a 20 nm cell answers `film1.thickness`, `film2.layer1.thickness` and `film2.layer2.thickness` in that order. `a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values`: ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes over the three elevated test-local inputs of step 206 MUST give those axes, names, kinds and defaults unchanged. Acceptance: After the vocabulary lands, `SourcePreset.parameterAxes` MUST publish the four light-source parameters at unpolarized unit scale, `PolarizerPreset.parameterAxes` none, `Sample.parameterAxes` one thickness per finite layer and `NoiseParam.parameterAxes` its three uncertainties; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale`, `an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter`, `a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer` and `a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
