    {
      "id": "S71-MODEL-FORMS",
      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7I ('Kit.Item = one PHYSICAL piece: ItemId (GUID) and an ItemLabel; the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted); its own Parameter values; optional photo (a kit file) and notes'; 'ItemModel \u2014 parameterised physics, a library entry (.item-model-json). Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated'; the model table; 'Parameter = a name plus a ParameterState: Known | Unknown of start * bounds * prior option | Calibrated of value * sigma * fromFitRun'; 'Dial mapping'; 'Revisions'; 'Material parameters as unknowns'), \u00a7A (library and kit extensions, the kit's flat root, module Kit), \u00a7B (entry files, schemas, the shipped catalogue, import), \u00a7C (the library proxies gain a SQLite create; contract tests; pinning), \u00a7E (library closure snapshot), \u00a7N, \u00a7P (AddItem, SetParameterState; KitProxy; every proxy has an in-memory stub), \u00a7Q (the bench noise model's types); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 23 (S7.1) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.3, \u00a73.11, \u00a73.14, \u00a73.17, \u00a73.23, \u00a74, \u00a75 (Kit module, ItemModel), \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79; specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7I; claim-check repair item 30; 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6 require complete item mapping before S7; shared prerequisites are scheduled in S6.",
      "requirement": "Step 208: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The parameterised item models of 001 \u00a7I as data, and the parameters each publishes (001 \u00a7I table; the S7.1 brief's payload rows; .spec-md \u00a73.14: every item MUST instantiate an ItemModel entry; source, ideal-polarizer and stack forms reuse the physics of step 207 through typed bindings). In `ItemModels.fs`, after step 207's extensions, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `Berreman.Fields` (`WaveLength`). (1) `PolarizerLeakage` = `ExtinctionRatioLeakage` (its parameter is the extinction ratio T_min / T_max) | `DiattenuationLeakage` (its parameter is the diattenuation (T_max \u2212 T_min) / (T_max + T_min)): how a real linear polarizer states its leakage. (2) `RetardanceDispersion` = `ConstantRetardance` (\u03b4 is the same at every \u03bb) | `InverseWaveLengthRetardance of WaveLength` (\u03b4 is the retardance at that reference \u03bb and scales as \u03bb_ref / \u03bb, a zero-order plate's dispersion): 'dispersive where the model says so'. (3) `BlackBoxNormalisation` = `SixteenElementMueller` (all sixteen elements are parameters) | `FifteenElementsAndScale` (a scale and the fifteen elements normalised by m00). (4) `OpticalForm` = `RealPolarizerModel of PolarizerLeakage` | `RetarderPlateModel of RetardanceDispersion` | `BlackBoxMuellerModel of BlackBoxNormalisation` | `CompoundModel of CompoundComponent list`, with `and CompoundComponent = { form : OpticalForm; offset : Angle }`: what one optical element does to light. A compound is its components in light order, each turned by its fixed offset within the compound, which generalises `ConstantMueller` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerBehavior`) with parameters (001 \u00a7I 'CPL = LP \u00b7 Retarder(axis = 45\u00b0 + \u0394, \u03b4)'). A black-box matrix is held at reference orientation and turned as R(\u2212\u03c6) M R(\u03c6) like any element (001 \u00a7I). (5) `ItemModelForm` = `SourcePresetItemModel` | `IdealPolarizerItemModel` | `StackSampleItemModel` | `OpticalElementModel of OpticalForm` | `EmptySlotModel` (the identity, the calibration reference) | `IntensityDetectorModel of ItemParameterAxis list` (records S\u2080 through a gain and a dark offset) | `MuellerPolarimeterModel of ItemParameterAxis list` (records a full Mueller matrix) | `EllipsometerModel of ItemParameterAxis list` (records \u03a8 and \u0394): the payload of an item-model library entry, a detector's budget being its noise axes' defaults. Evaluating a form to a Mueller matrix or a reading is the run law's (001 \u00a7N, S8.1), not this step's. (6) `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` on `OpticalForm` and on `ItemModelForm`. `RealPolarizerModel` publishes `extinctionRatio` (`FractionParameter`, 0) under `ExtinctionRatioLeakage` or `diattenuation` (`FractionParameter`, 1) under `DiattenuationLeakage`, then `axisOffset` (`AngleParameter`, 0), so its defaults are the ideal linear polarizer. `RetarderPlateModel` publishes `retardance` (`PhaseParameter`, \u03c0 / 2, a quarter wave) and `fastAxisOffset` (`AngleParameter`, 0) under either dispersion. `BlackBoxMuellerModel` publishes, under `SixteenElementMueller`, `m00` \u2026 `m33` (`m<row><column>`, row-major, `MuellerElementParameter`) at the identity, and under `FifteenElementsAndScale` `scale` (`ScaleParameter`, 1) followed by the fifteen `m<row><column>` other than `m00` at the identity. `CompoundModel` publishes, for its component k (1-based, light order), each axis of the component's form renamed `c<k>.<name>`, kind and default kept, so a compound inside a compound prefixes twice (`c2.c1.retardance`). `OpticalElementModel f` publishes `f`'s axes; `EmptySlotModel` publishes nothing; `IntensityDetectorModel noise` publishes `gain` (`ScaleParameter`, 1) and `darkOffset` (`ReadingParameter`, 0) followed by `noise` (step 207); `MuellerPolarimeterModel noise` and `EllipsometerModel noise` publish `noise`. The gain's session scope is the study's (001 \u00a7L, S11.1). Names are unique within a form. The source, ideal-polarizer and stack forms MUST declare the corresponding typed binding kind and derive their bound parameter axes by calling the SourcePreset, PolarizerPreset and Sample parameterAxes members from step 207; they MUST NOT copy those computations. Their unbound parameterAxes MUST contain no binding-dependent axes; the resolved choice in step 216 supplies them. No evaluator is added here. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests`, comparing names, kinds and defaults (angles within 1e-15): `a real linear polarizer publishes its leakage and its axis offset`: both leakages, defaults 0 and 1, then `axisOffset` 0. `a retarder plate publishes its retardance at a quarter wave and its fast-axis offset`: `retardance` \u03c0 / 2 and `fastAxisOffset` 0 under `ConstantRetardance` and under `InverseWaveLengthRetardance` of 632.8 nm (`WaveLength.nm`). `a compound publishes its components' parameters under their light-order prefixes` : the compound of a real LP by extinction ratio at 0\u00b0 and a constant retarder at 45\u00b0 publishes `c1.extinctionRatio`, `c1.axisOffset`, `c2.retardance` and `c2.fastAxisOffset` with the components' kinds and defaults; that compound as the second component of a compound after a black box publishes `c2.c1.extinctionRatio` among its names. `a black-box Mueller matrix publishes sixteen elements, or a scale and fifteen, at the identity`: sixteen names `m00` \u2026 `m33` with 1 on the diagonal and 0 elsewhere; `scale` then fifteen names without `m00`. `an empty slot publishes nothing and each detector its gain, dark offset and noise as its form says`: over `detectorNoiseAxes`, the intensity detector publishes `gain`, `darkOffset`, `rotationUncertainty`, `elementUncertainty` and `throughputUncertainty`, the polarimeter and the ellipsometer the last three, and `EmptySlotModel` `[]`. The detectorNoiseAxes fixture MUST use step 206's constructor over elevated test-local values; the list payload is the model's three noise axes. Every detector MUST publish that list unchanged. Acceptance: After the forms land, `ItemModelForm` MUST hold the optical element, empty slot and three detector forms, and every form's `parameterAxes` MUST publish the names, kinds and defaults specified, a compound's under `c<k>.` prefixes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a real linear polarizer publishes its leakage and its axis offset`, `a retarder plate publishes its retardance at a quarter wave and its fast-axis offset`, `a compound publishes its components' parameters under their light-order prefixes`, `a black-box Mueller matrix publishes sixteen elements, or a scale and fifteen, at the identity` and `an empty slot publishes nothing and each detector its gain, dark offset and noise as its form says`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel MUST also be serializable ItemModel forms whose bound axes reuse the named physics members.",
      "checks": [
