      "requirement": "Step 209: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model library store's seam in Domain: the entry, its identity, its errors, its record and its in-memory double, with a contract suite any store runs (001 \u00a7I '`ItemModel` \u2014 parameterised physics, a library entry'; 001 \u00a7C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite create', 'Contract tests'; the S7.1 brief: a proxy record, an in-memory implementation and a SQLite create, the S2 pattern; .spec-md \u00a73.3: built-ins are named through well-known ids). In `ItemModels.fs`, after step 208's forms, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `System` (`Guid`). (1) `ItemModelId of Guid` with `.value`, an item model's frozen GUID. `ItemModelVersionId = { itemModelId : ItemModelId; version : VersionNumber }`, one version of one item model, which an item pins (001 \u00a7I 'the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'). (2) `ItemModelEntry = { id : ItemModelId; name : EntryName; description : EntryDescription; model : ItemModelForm; protection : EntryProtection }`, shaped like `PolarizerPreset` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`): its protection derives from its provenance at the file seam (step 210). `ItemModelVersion = { version : VersionNumber; entry : ItemModelEntry }`, one stored version, with `member this.versionId : ItemModelVersionId`. (3) `module ItemModelIds`, shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`, no `[<Literal>]`, each a typed value written `Guid.Parse \"\u2026\" |> ItemModelId`), the frozen identities of the eleven built-in item models step 210 ships: `realLinearPolarizerModelId` `940bda4e-db9c-4103-b59c-dab2f3ee5875`; `retarderPlateModelId` `8e9797b7-f0db-443f-b33d-61f9901881cd`; `circularPolarizerModelId` `33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b`; `blackBoxMuellerModelId` `852cbb95-e9f