      "requirement": "Step 210: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item model becomes a library kind with its file, its schema and its import, and the built-in item models ship in the Built-in catalogue (001 \u00a7A 'Library extensions: \u2026 .item-model-json'; 001 \u00a7B; 001 \u00a7I; the S7.1 brief: LibraryEntryKind gains it, `.item-model-json` with a schema, CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel, the built-in item models are written once through the export path and added to Catalogue/Builtin/ with the manifest updated, and there is no code seed; .spec-md \u00a73.14; step 24: 'S7.1 adds the item-model kind'; step 57: a section that adds a built-in kind changes the integrity counts in the step that adds it). The kind, its rows and the facts that count them land together, because `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests` requires every kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all` to have rows. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (steps 24, 25, 137) opens `ItemModels`; each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (a) `LibraryEntryKind` gains `ItemModelEntryKind` after `CategoryEntryKind`: `value` 7 (`tryOfWire 7` answers it), extension `.item-model-json` (001 \u00a7A), schema version 1; `all` lists the seven in tag order, and its doc and step 24's 'S7.1 adds' remark say so. (b) Beside step 24's id extensions, `type ItemModelId with member this.toLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId`, the same GUID; after `EntryReference` (step 137), `type ItemModelVersionId with member this.entryReference : EntryReference`, the `EntryVersionReference` of that GUID at that version. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006). (c) `LibraryEntryPayload` gains `ItemModelPayload of ItemModelForm`, of kind `ItemModelEntryKind`. (d) The builder `static member ofItemModel (version : VersionNumber) (provenance : EntryProvenance) (entry : ItemModelEntry) : Result<LibraryEntryContent, LibraryEntryError>`, as step 25's preset builders: an `entry.protection` other than `provenance.protection` is `ProvenanceMismatchErr` naming the entry; otherwise the content holds the entry's id, name, `categoryOpt = None`, `descriptionOpt = Some entry.description` and `ItemModelPayload entry.model`. The decoder `member this.toItemModel : Result<ItemModelEntry, LibraryEntryError>` is marked as step 25's decoders are (`StorageBoundary`: the file's entry GUID becomes the item model's id): another payload is `EntryKindMismatchErr`, no description `MissingEntryFieldErr`, and the protection comes from the provenance. (e) `references` (step 137): an item model answers `[]`, because its components are inline forms, not entries. (2) Every match on `LibraryEntryKind` or `LibraryEntryPayload` the compiler now reports incomplete (FS0025 is an error) gains the case, and no wildcard is added. Among them: `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`' apply order (step 94: item models after detectors); `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs`' `schemaFile` and its per-kind lazies (step 30: `schema/library-item-model.schema.json`); `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`' `facetRows` (step 64: an item model has none); and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`' `LibraryEntryKind.caption` (step 107: `Item model`). (3) The import seam: the brief's 'CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel' is realised on step 94's kind-neutral seam. `InMemoryCatalogueStores` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`, built by `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` with `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()` (step 209). A put of an item-model id its map does not hold decodes the envelope with `toItemModel` and pushes `{ version = content.version; entry = \u2026 }` through `saveItemModel`, as step 94's adapters push the other kinds; `UndecodableEntryErr`, or an `ItemModelError` answered as `ImportRejectedErr` with its `describe`, stops the put before the map changes. The dat