ribed 'Records Psi and Delta, with the decent-lab noise budget.'. Their files are named by step 24's rule (`Real linear polarizer.item-model-json` and the rest, exactly this step's effects), LF-only, and `git check-ignore` reports none of them. Step 212 deletes the tool. (6) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains `itemModels () : ItemModelVersion list`, the catalogue's item-model rows decoded in row order at their versions, and `itemModel (id : ItemModelId) : ItemModelVersion`, failing with the id when the catalogue holds none, each with a one-line doc. (7) Tests. `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests`' `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present` (step 57) counts 11 item models beside its other kinds. It gains `the shipped item models include every required form under their well-known ids`: `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` holds exactly the eleven above by id, name and form, each at version 1 and `ProtectedBuiltIn`, and each envelope's provenance is `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension` (step 24) covers seven tags, `None` for 0 and 8, and `.item-model-json`. It gains `an item-model builder and decoder are inverse, and a protection its provenance disagrees with is refused`: a test-local `UserManaged` compound under `UserProvenance` decodes to itself through `ofItemModel` and `toItemModel`; a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry under `UserProvenance` answers `ProvenanceMismatchErr`; and `toItemModel` of Silicon's content answers `EntryKindMismatchErr`. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures` expects the tape to end with every item-model envelope, in row order, after the detectors. The same one-time 