      "requirement": "Step 211: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model store over the library database (001 \u00a7C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite create', 'Contract tests'; the S7.1 brief: a SQLite create with the contract suite run on both; step 76's pattern). New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ItemModelDatabaseStore.fs`, `module ItemModelDatabaseStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `PresetDatabaseStore.fs` (step 79): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type ItemModelProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : ItemModelProxy` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite item-model store (001 \u00a7C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]` and a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. As in step 76, every field is one `run` (step 62) over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. An item model is an entry whose latest row's kind is `ItemModelEntryKind`, built-in or user. `listItemModels ()` decodes (`toItemModel`, step 210) the latest version of every item model (`latestStoredOfKind ItemModelEntryKind`), whatever its lifecycle, as `{ version; entry }`, ordered by name and then by id. `resolveItemModelVersion v` answers `None` when `tryStoredVersion v.itemModelId.toLibraryEntryId v.version` finds no row or a row of another kind, and that version decoded otherwise. `saveItemModel v` answers `DuplicateItemModelErr` naming the id and its latest version when the id holds an item model; `InvalidItemModelErr` naming the id and that kind's `extension` when it holds another kind; `InvalidItemModelErr` carrying the builder's `describe` when `ofItemModel v.version UserProvenance v.entry` refuses, as it does a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry, because built-ins arrive only through the import seam (step 95); and otherwise it stages `stageNewEntry` of that content. No cache, retry, pin verb, removal or edit is added. Tests, in `ItemModelProxyTests.fs` (step 209): `type ItemModelProxySqliteTests () = inherit ItemModelProxyContract ()` runs the three contract facts over `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase` of an empty `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")` per store, and implements `IDisposable`, disposing every database it opened. Its own facts, each over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67) unless it says otherwise and each disposing it: `the database item-model store lists the Built-in item models and resolves each by its version` : `listItemModels` answers exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` (step 210) ordered by name, and `resolveItemModelVersion` of each one's `versionId` answers it. `the database item-model store holds user item models only and refuses an id it cannot hold`: a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry under a fresh GUID answers `InvalidItemModelErr`; an entry under the GUID of `MaterialIds.silicon` answers `InvalidItemModelErr` naming `.material-json`; an entry under `ItemModelIds.emptySlotModelId` answers `DuplicateItemModelErr`; and `tryLatestStored` of that built-in still answers the catalogue's envelope. `a database failure below the item-model store is ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr _)`. Acceptance: After the database store lands, `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase` MUST serve the library database's item models and save only user item models; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version`, `the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name` and `saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version` under `ItemModelProxySqliteTests`, and `the database item-model store lists the Built-in item models and resolves each by its version`, `the database item-model store holds user item models only and refuses an id it cannot hold` and `a database failure below the item-model store is ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
