      "requirement": "Step 212: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model entry file and the import of item models are proved over every form and over both stores (001 \u00a7B 'Any entry that cannot serialise is a test failure'; 001 \u00a7C 'Contract tests'; .spec-md \u00a79), and the export tool goes. No product source file changes. (0) The throw-away tool is deleted now that the shipped files and their facts are green (steps 210, 211), as step 36 deleted step 35's (.spec-md \u00a73.6; the S7.1 brief: written once, no code seed): `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` is removed, so `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/` holds only `Builtin/`. Nothing references it. (1) `EntryFileJsonTests` (step 30) gains `an item-model entry file round-trips every model form`: content \u2192 `sealed` \u2192 `fileText` \u2192 `parseEntry ItemModelEntryKind` answers an equal envelope whose `toItemModel` answers the entry, for test-local entries holding a real LP under each `PolarizerLeakage`, a retarder under `ConstantRetardance` and under `InverseWaveLengthRetardance` of 632.8 nm, a black box under each `BlackBoxNormalisation`, a compound whose second component is itself a compound, `EmptySlotModel`, and each detector over `detectorNoiseAxes` and over `zeroNoiseAxes`, under `BuiltInProvenance` and `UserProvenance`; and the real LP's file parsed as a `PolarizerEntryKind` answers `SchemaValidationErr`. (2) `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` (step 95): the test-local `ImportStoreSet` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`. `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` fills it with the `itemModels` of its `InMemoryCatalogueStores` (step 210), and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` with `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase` (step 211) of its database. The contract's `importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue` also requires `listItemModels` to answer one version per item-model row, and `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value` requires each item-model row's decoded version to be what `resolveItemModelVersion` answers for its `versionId`. Every other assertion is kept. detectorNoiseAxes MUST be the noise-axis list read from the shipped Mueller-polarimeter model; zeroNoiseAxes MUST be the same axis descriptors with every defaultValue set to the elevated zero. The serializer MUST round-trip lists of axes and MUST NOT bind a NoiseParam. The detector-model round-trip fact MUST assert integer kind tags on disk and reject zero and an unrecognized kind tag with the typed malformed-file error, while retaining all three noise defaults. Acceptance: After the facts land, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` MUST NOT exist and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/` MUST hold only `Builtin/`, every item-model form MUST round-trip through its entry file, and both import stores MUST hold and resolve the Built-in item models; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item-model entry file round-trips every model form` and `importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue` and `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value` under `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
