      "requirement": "Step 213: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. An item's identity and the model it instantiates, as pure Domain data in the `Kit` module (001 \u00a7I '`Kit.Item` = one PHYSICAL piece: `ItemId` (GUID) and an `ItemLabel` (`LP1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `Phone`); the `ItemModel` it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'; 001 \u00a7A: the kit module holds `Item`, `ItemId`, `ItemLabel`, `Parameter`, `ParameterState`; 001 \u00a7I: the model is always an ItemModel version, with an optional typed binding to preset or sample physics; .spec-md \u00a73.14, \u00a73.17, \u00a75 'Kit module'). `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs` (step 122) opens `ItemModels` (step 205), `Library` and `Placement`; the new types are appended at the end of the file in this order, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1, every case name of two words and no `bool`. (1) `ItemError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the item, the label or the parameter: `InvalidItemLabelErr` (a blank label), `DuplicateItemLabelErr` (another item of the kit has the label's file name), `DuplicateItemIdErr` (another item has the id), `UnknownItemParameterErr` (the item has no parameter of that name) and `InvalidParameterStateErr` (a parameter state breaks its rules, step 214). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the item label is not valid: <reason>`, `the kit already has an item of that label: <reason>`, `the kit already has an item of that id: <reason>`, `the item has no such parameter: <reason>` and `the parameter state is not valid: <reason>`. (2) `ItemId of Guid` with `.value`, one physical piece's frozen identity, minted by the caller as `KitId` is (step 122). (3) `ItemLabel of string` with `.value`. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<ItemLabel, ItemError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white