emModel version plus a separate physics binding reference; a standalone instance MUST return its model version and no binding.  `every item error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. ItemError MUST also declare UnknownKitItemErr of reason : string, rendered as `the kit has no item of that id: <reason>`, and the error-rendering fact MUST cover it; the S6 copy mapping requires this case. Acceptance: After the item identity lands, `ItemLabel.tryCreate` MUST refuse a blank label and name its file through the shared stem rule, and `ItemModelInstance.entryReferenceOpt` MUST answer the reference the kit snapshots; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item label keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `an item revision starts at one and counts up`, `an item's model is referenced as the library snapshots it` and `every item error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.",
