      "requirement": "Step 214: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. A parameter and its state (001 \u00a7I '`Parameter` = a name plus a `ParameterState`: `Known of value` | `Unknown of start * bounds * prior option` | `Calibrated of value * sigma * fromFitRun`'; the S7.1 brief: the name REUSES `ParameterName`; .spec-md \u00a73.17: the cases are `KnownParameter`, `UnknownParameter` and `CalibratedParameter`). In `Kit.fs`, after `ItemModelInstance` (step 213), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ParameterInterval = { lower : ParameterValue; upper : ParameterValue }`, the bounds a fit searches within. (2) `ParameterSigma of double` with `.value`, one standard deviation in the parameter's unit. (3) `ParameterPrior = { centre : ParameterValue; sigma : ParameterSigma }`, a Gaussian prior. (4) `UnknownParameterData = { start : ParameterValue; bounds : ParameterInterval; priorOpt : ParameterPrior option }`. (5) `FitRunName of string` with `.value`, the fit run a calibration came from, named by its file stem `<study>@<stamp>` (001 \u00a7A); S11.3 writes fit runs under it and S11.5 publishes from them. (6) `CalibratedParameterData = { value : ParameterValue; sigma : ParameterSigma; fitRun : FitRunName }`. Records hold the same-typed pairs, because a case tuple repeating a type is ELEV011. (7) `ParameterState` = `KnownParameter of ParameterValue` | `UnknownParameter of UnknownParameterData` | `CalibratedParameter of CalibratedParameterData`. (8) `Parameter = { name : ParameterName; state : ParameterState }`. `static member knownAtDefault (axis : ItemParameterAxis) : Parameter` is the axis's name with `KnownParameter axis.defaultValue`, the one way an item's parameters are made from a model's axes (step 216). `member this.validate : Result<Parameter, ItemError>` answers the parameter when its state keeps the rules and otherwise `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming the parameter and the broken rule: every number is finite (neither NaN nor infinite); an unknown's `bounds.lower` is below its `bounds.upper` and its `start` lies within them, ends included; a prior's and a calibration's `sigma` is above zero. No range by kind is checked here, because a kind's range is its model's (S8.1). No other type or member is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests` (step 213): `a parameter is created known at its axis default`: `Parameter.knownAtDefault` of the `retardance` axis that `(OpticalElementModel (RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance)).parameterAxes` publishes is named `retardance` and `KnownParameter` of \u03c0 / 2. `a parameter whose state keeps its rules is kept, and one that breaks them is InvalidParameterStateErr`: a known 0.1, an unknown starting at 0.5 within [0, 1] with and without a prior of centre 0.5 and sigma 0.1, an unknown starting on its lower bound, and a calibration of 0.25 with sigma 0.01 from `FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\"` each validate to themselves; a known NaN, an unknown whose bounds are [1, 1], an unknown starting at \u22120.5 within [0, 1], a prior with sigma 0 and a calibration with sigma \u22121 each answer `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming the parameter. Acceptance: After the parameter states land, `Parameter.knownAtDefault` MUST make a known parameter at the axis's default and `Parameter.validate` MUST refuse a non-finite number, an empty or misplaced search interval and a non-positive sigma; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a parameter is created known at its axis default` and `a parameter whose state keeps its rules is kept, and one that breaks them is InvalidParameterStateErr`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
