      "requirement": "Step 215: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item itself, with its dial mapping and its revision history (001 \u00a7I: an item has its own `Parameter` values, an optional photo (a kit file) and notes; 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (`DialSign` exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; 'Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history'; the S7.1 brief). In `Kit.fs`, after `Parameter` (step 214), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ItemDial` = `DialMounted of DialSign` (the item turns on a dial: a raw reading maps to the physical angle as `sign \u00b7 (reading \u2212 dialZero)`, the rule of `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle`) | `FixedMounting` (the item is not read off a dial). `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` answers, for `DialMounted`, the one axis `dialZero` (`AngleParameter`, 0), and `[]` for `FixedMounting`, so the zero is an ordinary parameter of the item. (2) `ItemRevisionRecord = { revision : ItemRevision; parameters : Parameter list }`, the values an earlier revision held: the short value history (fit runs keep every vector, 001 \u00a7I). (3) `Item = { id : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; model : ItemModelInstance; parameters : Parameter list; dial : ItemDial; photoOpt : KitRelativePath option; notes : ItemNotes; revision : ItemRevision; history : ItemRevisionRecord list }`. The photo is a kit-relative path to a kit file (step 123). `history` lists earlier revisions, oldest first. `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list` MUST be its model's exact entryReferenceOpt followed by bindingReferenceOpt when present, with duplicate references removed: what the kit snapshots and pins when it records the item (step 219). `member this.tryFindParameter (name : ParameterName) : Parameter op