      "requirement": "Step 216: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Adding an item, as a pure update over the kit's items (001 \u00a7P: `AddItem` is a semantic message; the S7.1 brief: pure updates for AddItem, an item's parameters are created from the generated axes; 001 \u00a7I 'Two LPs of one model are two items with independent parameters'). In `Kit.fs`, after `Item` (step 215), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ItemModelChoice` = `SourcePresetChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * source : SourcePreset` | `PolarizerPresetChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * polarizer : PolarizerPreset` | `StackSampleChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * version : SampleVersionId * sample : Sample` | `LibraryModelChoice of ItemModelVersion`: a model as the library resolved it. `member this.instance : ItemModelInstance` MUST carry the choice's exact model version in every case: PresetInstance (model.versionId, preset.id), SampleInstance (model.versionId, version), or ItemModelVersionInstance model.versionId; `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` MUST match the model form and typed binding, calling the preset/sample parameterAxes members (step 207) for SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel, or entry.model.parameterAxes for a standalone form (step 208). (2) `ItemDraft = { id : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; model : ItemModelChoice; dial : ItemDial }`, what `AddItem` gives. `member this.toItem : Item` holds the draft's id, label, `model.instance` and dial; its `parameters` are `Parameter.knownAtDefault` (step 214) of `model.parameterAxes` followed by `dial.parameterAxes`, in that order; `photoOpt = None`, `notes = ItemNotes \"\"`, `revision = ItemRevision.first` and `history = []`. `member this.addTo (items : Item list) : Result<Item, ItemError>` answers `DuplicateItemIdErr` when an item holds the id, `Dupli