d that sample version. `two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters`: LP1 and LP2, two drafts over the `ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId` model with distinct test-local ids, are two items whose parameters are equal and whose ids and labels differ. `adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused`: over a kit holding LP1, a draft labelled `lp1`, and one labelled `LP:1` beside an item labelled `LP_1`, answer `DuplicateItemLabelErr`, and a draft reusing LP1's id answers `DuplicateItemIdErr`. Acceptance: After AddItem lands, `ItemDraft.toItem` MUST create every parameter its model and dial publish, known at its default, at revision 1, and `ItemDraft.addTo` MUST refuse an id or a label file name the kit already holds; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `adding an item from a library model creates its parameters known at the model's defaults and its dial zero`, `a source preset, an ideal polarizer and a sample give an item their own parameters`, `two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters` and `adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.",
