      "requirement": "Step 234: Setting one parameter's state, as a pure update of one item (001 \u00a7P: `SetParameterState` is a semantic message; the S7.1 brief: pure updates for SetParameterState; 001 \u00a7I: each item has its own parameter values). On `Item` in `Kit.fs` (step 215), documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `member this.withParameterState (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<Item, ItemError>`. It answers `UnknownItemParameterErr` naming the item's label and the name when no parameter has the name, and the `InvalidParameterStateErr` of `{ name = name; state = state }.validate` (step 214) when the state breaks its rules; otherwise the item with that parameter's state replaced in place, every other parameter, the order, the revision and the history unchanged. A state set this way edits the working revision; only a published revision (step 235) moves the revision. It writes nothing. Tests, in `KitItemTests`, over a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` (step 216): `setting a parameter's state replaces it in place and keeps the revision`: setting `c2.retardance` to `UnknownParameter` starting at \u03c0 / 2 within [\u03c0 / 4, 3\u03c0 / 4] answers the item with that state at the same position, the other four parameters unchanged and revision 1. `setting the state of a parameter the item lacks, or one that breaks its rules, is refused`: setting `nothing`, and setting `c2.retardance` to an unknown whose bounds are reversed, answer `UnknownItemParameterErr` and `InvalidParameterStateErr`, and the item is as it was. `two items of one model keep independent parameters` : with CPL2 made by the same draft under another id and label, setting CPL1's `c2.fastAxisOffset` to `KnownParameter 0.01` leaves CPL2's parameters equal to the model's defaults. Acceptance: After SetParameterState lands, `Item.with