      "requirement": "Step 217: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. An item persists as its own kit file, `<label>.item-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema (001 \u00a7A 'Kit extensions \u2026 .item-json', 'A file that exists many times is named by its own identity'; the S7.1 brief: `<label>.item-json` kit files go through KitProxy with a schema and a version; .spec-md \u00a74 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`); no second parser or writer is written. (1) `Kit.fs`, after Item (step 215), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `ItemFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; item : Item }`, the `.item-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1, and `type Item with member this.itemFile : ItemFile`, the item at the current schema version. A file is read back as its `item` field; no member converts the other way (ELEV006). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/item.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/experiment.schema.json` (step 146), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/item.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `item`; `item` holds exactly `id` (the GUID definition of `library-common.schema.json`, referenced by its `$id`), `label` (a non-empty string), `model`, `parameters` (an array), `dial`, `photoOpt` (`null` or a non-empty string), `notes` (a string), `revision` (a positive integer) and `history` (an array). The model, parameters, dial and history are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one, as step 146's descriptors are. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/experiment.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateItemFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateExperimentFile` (step 146) does. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs` (step 146): `type ItemFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`, and `type KitFileText with member this.parseItemFile : Result<ItemFile, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateItemFile ItemKitFile.extension ItemFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value` (steps 123, 124). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests, in `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146): `an item is stored under its label`: `ItemKitFile.fileNameOf` of `(ItemLabel \"CPL1\").fileStem` is `FileName \"CPL1.item-json\"`. `an item file round-trips through its canonical text`: a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive`, with its record initialized to revision 2, c2.retardance unknown under a prior, c2.fastAxisOffset calibrated, the revision-1 parameters in history, a photoOpt of data/photos/CPL1.jpg and notes, and a laser item over `PresetIds.heNe633` with `FixedMounting`, each go `itemFile`, `fileText`, then `parseItemFile` and answer an equal file; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys as `item` then `schemaVersion`, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text. `an item file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` : CPL1's text with `schemaVersion` 2, with its body and as `{ \"schemaVersion\": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = ItemKitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed item file is refused before it binds`: CPL1's text without `item`, with an extra top-level key `notes`, with `item.label` empty, and with `item.revision` 0 each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance. Acceptance: After the item file lands, `ItemFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseItemFile` reads back equal, validated against `schema/item.schema.json`, another schema version being `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item is stored under its label`, `an item file round-trips through its canonical text`, `an item file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` and `a schema-invalid or malformed item file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
