      "requirement": "Step 218: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. A kit's items are read and written by typed members over the per-kind verbs (001 \u00a7P '`KitProxy` \u2026 kit, items, \u2026'; step 127: a kind adds no proxy verb; step 148's members for experiments). In `KitContentFiles.fs`, on step 148's `type KitProxy with` extension, each member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: (1) `member this.writeItem (item : Item) : Result<unit, KitError>` renders `item.itemFile.fileText` (step 217) and writes it with `writeKindFile ItemKitFile item.label.fileStem`, replacing a file of that name whole; a `StorageError` of the rendering is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the error's `describe`. (2) `member this.readItems () : Result<Item list, KitError>` reads every stem `listKindFiles ItemKitFile` answers, with `readKindFile`, and parses it with `parseItemFile`. A refusal, a file whose item's `label.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case, or a second file holding an `ItemId` already read is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason, and the whole read answers it, so a kit never opens with an item left out. The answer is ordered by the label's text (ordinal). Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) a write answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and a read passes, because the members call the proxy's verbs. No delete, cache, retry or other member is added; an item is renamed by no member in this section. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs`, `module KitItemFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitItemFileTests\", <a new GUID>)`, build `KitProxy.create` over it and call `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (the `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` precedent, step 148). Its items are CPL1, LP1 and Phone made through `ItemDraft.toItem` (step 216) over the circular-polarizer, real-LP and intensity-detector built-ins. `a kit's item files round-trip, each stored under its label` : after `writeItem` of Phone, CPL1 and LP1, the folder holds `CPL1.item-json`, `LP1.item-json` and `Phone.item-json`, and `readItems` answers CPL1, LP1 and Phone in that order. `writing an item again under its label replaces its file`: CPL1, then a CPL1 record initialized with revision 2 and its prior parameters in history, reads back as the second. This storage fact MUST construct the record directly and MUST NOT depend on the publication behavior introduced in step 235. `an item file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refuses the read, naming the file`: `Broken.item-json` written by the test as `{`, `Other.item-json` holding CPL1's file text, and `CPL9.item-json` holding a file whose item is labelled `CPL9` but has LP1's id each make `readItems` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file. `a read-only kit refuses an item write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `writeItem` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`, the folder's files and bytes are unchanged, and `readItems` answers what the kit holds. Acceptance: After the typed members land, `KitProxy.writeItem` MUST write each item to `<label>.item-json` and `KitProxy.readItems` MUST read every item file back, ordered by label, a file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refusing the whole read; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's item files round-trip, each stored under its label`, `writing an item again under its label replaces its file`, `an item file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refuses the read, naming the file` and `a read-only kit refuses an item write and writes nothing`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
