nd their categories`: a QZ item over `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 snapshots the sample, its glass material and that material's category, each once. `recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version`: a laser item over `SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.heNe633` snapshots that preset's version 1. `a read-only kit records no item`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, `recordItem` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance. Acceptance: After recording lands, `KitLibraryContext.recordItem` MUST snapshot and pin the library version an item's model names, with its closure, before it writes the item's file, and write nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recording an item snapshots its model's library version and pins it, then writes its file`, `recording a sample item snapshots the sample with its materials and their categories`, `recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version` and `a read-only kit records no 