      "requirement": "Step 221: S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 \u00a7H and \u00a7S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item mapping of Copy experiments from another kit\u2026 as pure data (001 \u00a7H 'brings the experiments with their setups, data files and the items they use. Items map onto existing items where the user says so; otherwise they are added'; .spec-md \u00a73.15: the item mapping MUST be complete in S6; the S7.2 brief: a mapping table lists every item the picked experiments use, each with 'map to existing item' or 'add', the default mapping by identical model and label and otherwise adding; the S7.1 mapper's request: items map by `ItemId` or label). Each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after the Item declarations from step 215. (a) `type ItemLabel with member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : ItemLabel list) : ItemLabel` answers the first of `<label>`, `<label> (2)`, `<label> (3)`, \u2026 whose `fileStem` no label of `taken` has, ignoring case: the suffix form of `KitDataFolder.copyTargetFor` (step 132) on a label, because an item's file is named by its label (step 217). (b) `ItemCopyChoice` = `MapOntoKitItem of ItemId` (the copy uses the target kit's item of that id and brings nothing) | `AddCopiedItem` (the source item is added to the target kit). `ItemCopyRow = { sourceItem : Item; choice : ItemCopyChoice }`, one row of the mapping table. Neither is stored, so neither carries a wire tag. (c) `type Item with member this.defaultCopyChoice (held : Item list) : ItemCopyChoice` is `MapOntoKitItem` of the held item with this item's `id` when there is one, because one id is one physical piece (001 \u00a7I); otherwise `MapOntoKitItem` of the first held item whose `model` equals this item's and whose `label` equals its label (ordinal); otherwise `AddCopiedItem`. (d) On `ItemCopyRow`, `static member copyRowsFor (used : Item list) (held : Item list) (chosen : ItemCopyRow list) : ItemCopyRow list` answers one row per item of `used`, in order, whose choice is that of the `chosen` row with the same `sourceItem.id`, or else the item's `defaultCopyChoice held`: the panel keeps what the user chose while the chosen experiments change, and a copy given no row takes the defaults. (e) On `ItemCopyRow`, `static member itemsToAdd (rows : ItemCopyRow list) (held : Item list) : Result<Item list, ItemError>` checks every row before it answers: a `MapOntoKitItem id` whose `id` no held item has is `UnknownKitItemErr` (step 213) naming the source item's label and the id; an `AddCopiedItem` of an item whose `id` a held item has is `DuplicateItemIdErr` naming its label, because a piece the kit holds is mapped, not added twice. Otherwise it answers the `AddCopiedItem` rows' items in order, each relabelled `label.nextFreeAmong` the held labels and the labels given to the earlier added items, every other field kept. (2) In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, `ElementDescriptor` MUST gain `itemIdOpt : ItemId option`, the physical item explicitly captured at that element, separate from its library `binding`. `None` MUST mean no physical item was assigned; matching a model, preset, label or library reference MUST NOT infer an identity. `Experiment.itemsUsedBy (experiments : Experiment list) (items : Item list) : Result<Item list, ItemError>` MUST resolve every Some id from the descriptors against the supplied items, return the referenced items once in the supplied item order, and return UnknownKitItemErr naming the missing id and descriptor on a dangling reference. A standalone item-model item MUST be usable in S6 by its id. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json` and `KitContentFiles.fs` MUST serialize that option with the canonical F# option representation, require the field and validate its GUID payload; incompatible older bodies MUST be refused by the schema with no fallback reader or inferred binding. `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` and `KitContentFileJsonTests` MUST construct physical fixtures with their actual ItemIds at origin and use None only for deliberately unassigned descriptors. `ExperimentDataLoad.fs` and `SolverHandoffView.fs` MUST compile against the enlarged descriptor, retaining their detector and validation behavior. The inventory still lists ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs as a descriptor consumer: its exact path MUST remain in scope solely to preserve the deletion at step 152; an absent file MUST remain absent and no test MAY be recreated. (4) In `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:model.experimentSetup`, a recaptured descriptor of the currently edited experiment MUST retain that experiment's itemIdOpt for the same elementId when its library binding is unchanged; a new or rebound element MUST carry None. This preserves copied physical identity on edit without guessing from a preset. In `InverseConstructorTests`, `recommitting a copied experiment preserves its assigned physical ids` MUST load an experiment with two same-preset pieces, edit and commit it, reopen the folder and assert both distinct ids remain. No second parser or copy-only durable format MAY be introduced. Tests. In `KitItemTests`: `an added item's label takes the next free suffix among the labels the kit holds`: `CPL1` among `cpl1` and `CPL1 (2)` answers `CPL1 (3)`, among no label `CPL1`, and `LP:1` among `LP_1` answers `LP:1 (2)`. `an item maps by default onto the kit's item of its id, then of its model and label, and is otherwise added`: with the held items LP1 (real-LP model) and CPL1 (circular-polarizer model), a source item of LP1's id labelled `Polarizer A` maps onto LP1; a source `CPL1` of the circular-polarizer model under another id maps onto the held CPL1; a source `CPL1` of the real-LP model and a source `CPL2` of the circular-polarizer model are added. `the mapping rows follow the used items and keep the choices already made`: `copyRowsFor` of the used items LP1 and QZ, with a chosen row adding QZ, answers LP1 at its default and QZ added, in that order; a chosen row of an item not used gives no row. `the items to add are checked before any is answered, and each clashing label is suffixed`: over held `CPL1`, an added source `CPL1` is `CPL1 (2)` and a second added `CPL1` `CPL1 (3)`; an added item whose id the kit holds answers `DuplicateItemIdErr`, a mapping onto an id the kit lacks `UnknownKitItemErr`, and either refusal answers no item. In `ExperimentProxyTests`, `the items an experiment uses are its explicit physical ids, each once` MUST use Laser, QZ-A and QZ-B, where QZ-A and QZ-B share the exact model and sample version but have distinct ids and parameters. An experiment explicitly binding Laser and QZ-B MUST resolve exactly those items and exclude QZ-A; repeated references MUST resolve QZ-B once; an unassigned descriptor MUST use none; a descriptor naming a standalone CPL item model MUST resolve that item immediately. `a missing physical item is refused instead of guessed from a shared preset` MUST use a well-formed descriptor with a missing ItemId plus a held same-preset item and assert UnknownKitItemErr. In `KitContentFileJsonTests`, `experiment files preserve distinct same-preset physical ids and reject an omitted identity field` MUST round-trip two assigned descriptors, assert the exact ids and order, then remove the required field from otherwise valid JSON and assert SchemaValidationErr. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Acceptance: After S6 identity binding lands, experiment files MUST pre