der against EMPTY in-memory stores and seam (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, step 95), resolves both versions through `(ItemModelProxy .createInMemory ()).overlaidWith` of its `openOverlay []` (step 142), each equal to `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel` of its id, and `listItemModels` answers the two, by name. `the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through`: over the Built-in library, for a kit whose snapshot of the circular polarizer at version 1 has another description, `resolveItemModelVersion` of that version answers the kit's description, `listItemModels` answers the store's eight item models and no second circular polarizer, and `saveItemModel` of a test-local user item model through the overlaid store holds it in the underlying store. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance. Acceptance: After the overlay lands, `ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith` MUST answer a kit's snapshot-only item model and the kit's copy of a divergent version, list the store's item models first and pass a save to the store; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's item models resolve from its snapshots against an empty library` and `the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.",
