equence step 221 wrote into `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong`, moved here, and `nextFreeAmong`'s body becomes the `ItemLabel` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken labels' `fileStem`s, so one sequence serves items and setups (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). A member may speak its type's primitives (AGENTS.md). (b) Appended at the end of the file, in this order, every case name of two words and no `bool`: `SetupError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the setup, the revision, the slot or the item: `InvalidSetupNameErr` (a blank name), `DuplicateSetupNameErr` (another setup of the kit has the name's file stem), `UnknownSetupErr` (the kit holds no setup of that name), `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` (the setup holds no such revision), `UnknownSetupSlotErr` (the table has no slot of that element), `UnknownSlotItemErr` (the kit holds no item of that id, or the library no model of it) and `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` (the item's model does not fit the slot's kind); `member this.describe : string` renders them `the setup name is not valid: <reason>`, `the kit already has a setup of that name: <reason>`, `the kit has no such setup: <reason>`, `the setup has no such revision: <reason>`, `the table has no such slot: <reason>`, `the item is not available: <reason>` and `the item does not fit the slot: <reason>`. `SetupName of string` with `.value`: `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<SetupName, SetupError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white-space text with `InvalidSetupNameErr`; `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value`, the stem of its `<name>.setup-json` (001 \u00a7A), so a name keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md \u00a73.11, step 147's rule); `member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : SetupName list) : SetupName` is the `SetupName` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken names' `fileStem`s; `static member firstFree (taken : SetupName list) : SetupName` is the first of `Setup 1`