      "id": "S82-SETUP-SHAPE",
      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7J ('Setup = an ordered optical path of slots, each holding an item or nothing: Source, Prep 1\u2026k, Object 1\u2026n (two or more samples in series), Analyzer 1\u2026k, Detector; per slot: position on the beam, R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading. The table draws the active setup, and the BeamLayout / RayModel laws are unchanged'; 'Experiments reference setups (name + revision). The ElementDescriptor list becomes the slot list'; 'Quick swap: \u2026 choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'), \u00a7P (CreateSetup, AssignSlot, SwapSlot), \u00a7I ('Dial mapping \u2026 Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'), \u00a7A ('.setup-json'), \u00a7H ('Between kits'), \u00a7N ('The run law walks any number of objects', 'The source is real'); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 26 (S8.2) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a70.1 (Experiments.fs, Scene.fs, TableAndElementRotationView.fs rows), \u00a73.11, \u00a73.15, \u00a74, \u00a75 (Setup, SetupName, slots), \u00a76 (Version rule), \u00a77, \u00a78, \u00a79",
      "requirement": "Step 256: A setup as Domain data: an ordered optical path of slots, each slot one element of the table holding an item or nothing, and the revisions an experiment can reference (001 \u00a7J; the S8.2 brief: `Setup { name : SetupName; revision; slots }`, each slot holding an item (`ItemId`) or nothing plus its position on the beam and R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading; 'Experiments keep their captured-snapshot meaning through the setup revision: editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision'; .spec-md \u00a75, \u00a76 'Version rule'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`: `module Setups` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `BeamLayout.fs`, because a slot sits on a `BeamLayout.BeamHost`: one `<Compile Include=\"Setups.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the setup, an ordered optical path of slots that the table draws (spec 0050 S8.2). It opens `Placement`, `Kit`, `ItemModels`, `Lifecycle` and `LibraryEntryFiles`; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (2) `SlotTurn` = `PlacementTurn` (the slot's R1 is its placement's own) | `DialTurn of reading : Angle` (the slot's item turns on a dial set to this raw reading, and its R1 is the item's `DialSign.physicalAngleOf` of it, step 255). `SlotContent` = `EmptySlotContent` | `ItemInSlot of item : ItemId * turn : SlotTurn`, with `member this.itemOpt : ItemId option`. (3) `SetupSlot = { id : Library.ElementId; placement : ElementPlacement; zoom : BeamLayout.ElementZoom; beam : BeamLayout.BeamHost; content : SlotContent }`, one slot of a setup and the one table element that draws it: its stable id (an experiment's varied element names it), its placement (the catalogue kind, the position along its beam, R1 / R2 / R3, the locks, the emission and the library entry it is bound to, `Placement.fs:ElementPlacement`), its draw zoom, the beam it sits on and its content. It carries wh