eVersioning`, the one version rule) over `{ physics = this.slots; metadata = () }` and `{ physics = slots; metadata = () }` with `pin` (step 65's `PinState`): `KeepCurrent` answers the setup unchanged, `MutateInPlace` the setup holding `slots`, and `MintNextVersion` the setup at `revision.next` holding `slots`, its current revision and slots appended to `history`. A setup has no metadata beyond its name, so its slots alone decide. No cache, wire tag or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs`, `module SetupTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its fixture slots are test-local records over `ElementPlacement.create` (`Placement.fs`), zoom `BeamLayout.ElementZoom 5.0` and `BeamLayout.OnMainBeam`: `src` (`LightSource` at `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint`), `lp` (`LinearPolarizer` at x = \u22120.3 m) and `det` (`Detector` at `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`), each `EmptySlotContent`, and a test-local `ItemId`. `a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds`: `lp.layoutElement` holds `lp`'s id, placement, beam as `host` and zoom; `itemOpt` of `ItemInSlot (item, PlacementTurn)` is `Some item` and of `EmptySlotContent` `None`. `a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had`: a setup `Bench` at revision 3 with history records r1 and r2 of distinct slot lists answers each list at its revision, and revision 4 answers `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` whose reason names `'Bench' revision 4`. `a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order`: a setup whose current slots hold items A then B and whose history holds B then C lists A, B, C. `a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused`: `create (SetupName \"Bench\")` over no held setup is revision 1 with no history; over a held `bench` it answers `DuplicateSetupNameErr`, and `Bench: A` over a held `Bench_ A` too. `a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next`: revising with equal slots answers the setup unchanged, pinned or not; with `lp` turned to R1 30\u00b0 and `VersionUnpinned` the revision and history are unchanged and the slots are the new ones; with `VersionPinned` the setup is at revision 2 with the new slots and one history record holding revision 1 and the old slots; a second pinned change gives revision 3 with history r1 then r2. Acceptance: After the setup shape lands, `Setups.fs` MUST hold `SlotTurn`, `SlotContent`, `SetupSlot`, `SetupRevisionRecord` and `Setup`, a setup MUST answer its slots at each revision it holds and refuse others, and `revisedWith` MUST mint the next revision exactly when the revision is pinned and the slots change; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds`, `a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had`, `a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order`, `a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused` and `a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.",
