l ignoring case; otherwise the item whose label equals the part ignoring case. A part naming no item answers `UnknownNameItemErr` naming the part and the placeholder's `text`. Item labels are unique by file stem ignoring case (step 216), so at most one item matches. (c) `member this.setupNameOf (slots : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) : Result<SetupName, NamingTemplateError>` is `writeName` of `nameReadingOf slots items None`, made a `SetupName` by `toSetupName`; a blank name answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming the template. (d) `member this.setupNameAmong (slots : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (taken : SetupName list) (unnamed : SetupName) : SetupName` is `setupNameOf`'s name made free among `taken` by `nextFreeAmong` (step 255), or `unnamed` when the template cannot name the slots. It names every new setup the window and the grid make (steps 272 and 276), `unnamed` being S8.2's name for it. Setups and experiments keep their names when the template changes: a template names what is made after it is saved. No other member, cache or option is added. Tests, in `NamingTemplateTests`, over slots made as `SetupTests` makes them (steps 256-258): `src` (a `LightSource` at `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint`), `lpA` (a `LinearPolarizer` at x \u22120.3 m), `sampleA` (a `Sample` at x \u22120.1 m), `sampleB` (a `Sample` at x 0.1 m), `lpB` (a `LinearPolarizer` at x 0.3 m) and `det` (a `Detector` at `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`), all on the main beam; test-local items made through `ItemDraft` (step 216), each `FixedMounting` unless named: `Laser` (`PresetIds.heNe633`), `CPL1` and `CPL2` (`ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId`), `QZ`, `LR` and `QZd` (`ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId`, `QZd` `DialMounted DialNegative` with its `dialZero` known at 10\u00b0), each put in its slot by `withItem` (step 258) after the slot's R1 is set; and the template `lab` = `tryCreate \"{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL,LP2=LP}-{note}\"`. `a setup's name is written from its slots in light order, its items under their aliases and its objects at their angles`: `src` holding `Laser`, `lpA` `CPL1`, `sampleA` `QZ` at R1 45\u00b0, `sampleB` `LR` at 45\u00b0, `lpB` `CPL2` and `det` nothing is named `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` by `lab` and `CPL1-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL2` by `NamingTemplate.standard`; with `sampleB` holding nothing, `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`; with `QZd` in `sampleA` at R1 30\u00b0 (its reading \u221220\u00b0, step 258) and `sampleB` holding nothing, `CPL-(QZd#-20)-CPL`; and `nameReadingOf` with the note `2`, written by `writeName`, is `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`. `a name reads back into the items of its slots and their angles`: `itemsOf` of `lab`'s reading of `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` over those items is `CPL1` at `PrepSlotRole 1`, `QZ` at `ObjectSlotRole 1`, `LR` at `ObjectSlotRole 2` and `CPL2` at `AnalyzerSlotRole 1`, with the angles 45\u00b0 and 45\u00b0; the object part `qz` reads as `QZ`; and `CPL-(XX#45)-CPL` answers `UnknownNameItemErr` naming `XX` and `obj1`. `writing a setup's name and reading it back gives its items and angles`: for each slot list of the first fact and for one with `sampleA` at 22.5\u00b0, the slots' items by role equal `itemsOf` of the `readName` of their `setupNameOf`, and each object's angle equals the read angle within 1e-12. `a setup the template cannot name says which placeholder is empty, and a new setup takes the template's name made free, or the name it is given`: with `lpA` holding nothing, `setupNameOf` answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming `source1` and `setupNameAmong \u2026 [] (SetupName \"Setup 3\")` answers `Setup 3`; the full slots among `[]` answer `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, and among `cpl-(qz#45-lr#45)-cpl` `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL (2)`. Acceptance: After names come from slots, `NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf`, `itemsOf`, `setupNameOf` and `setupNameAmong`, `SlotItem`, `ItemLabel.namePart` and `NameText.toSetupName` MUST exist in `NamingTemplates.fs`, a setup's name MUST be written f