      "requirement": "Step 276: `GenerateSetupGrid` as a semantic message: every ticked combination becomes a setup of the kit, with an experiment of the draft over each, at once (001 \u00a7J 'all setups and experiments created at once'; 001 \u00a7P `GenerateSetupGrid`; the grid's controls, `SetupGridGenerateButton`, are S8.4's). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `GenerateSetupGrid of SetupGrids.SetupGrid`, with a one-line doc: every ticked combination of the grid over the table, as setups and experiments of the kit. Its arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185. Otherwise it calls `grid.generate model.elements model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate model.kitSetups` (steps 274, 263): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Not generated \u2014 <e.describe>` and writes nothing. `Ok setups`: each setup not in `kitSetups` (by equality) is recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260), in order; then, when the draft has a capture (`model.draftCapture`, as `ExpCommit` reads it), the collection takes it (`chooseMeasurement`) and `commitOverSetups` (step 275) over the setups' references in order, and each experiment it appends is recorded as `ExpCommit` records one (step 261). The first write that fails stops the run: `kitSetups` and the collection hold what was written, and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit \u2014 <e.describe>`. On success `kitSetups` holds the new setups in name order and `kitStatus` is `Generated <n> setups (<m> new) and <k> experiments.`. The table, `activeSetupOpt` and the draft's fields are unchanged. (2) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'The table is the active setup' (step 261), one bullet of at most six lines: **Names come from the kit's naming template** (`NamingTemplates.fs`, spec 0050 S8.3): `{source}` is the polarization source (Prep 1), `{light}` the light source, `{obj<k>}` / `{phi<k>}` the objects and their angles (a dial reading or R1), then `{analyzer}`, `{detector}` and `{note}`; a second or later slot of a role and the note are left out with the text before them, and `{source:CPL1=CPL}` writes an item under another name. A new setup takes the template's name made free (`setupNameAmong`), and one the template cannot name keeps `Setup <n>`; the reference pipeline reads the lab's labels through `NamingTemplate.standard`, and the grid generator is `SetupGrids.fs`. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests`, over step 272's table (`LP1`, the sample, `LPd`) with the first polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and a grid made by `SetupGrid.create` over the sample's options `QZ` at 0\u00b0, `QZ` at 45\u00b0 and `QZ2` at 0\u00b0 with (`QZ2`, 0\u00b0) unticked: `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each`: the kit holds `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd.setup-json` and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` at revision 1 and `E1` and `E2` referencing them in that order, with the draft's variable; `kitStatus` is `Generated 2 setups (2 new) and 2 experiments.`; and `elements` and `activeSetupOpt` are as they were. `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing`: the same grid again leaves both setup files' bytes unchanged, records `E3` and `E4` over them and sets `Generated 2 setups (0 new) and 2 experiments.`; a grid record whose sample options hold `Laser` and whose `unticked` is empty sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not generated` and naming `Laser`, and no kit file changes. `a grid over a draft that cannot be committed records its setups and no experiment`: after `ExpNew` (no element chosen) the grid writes the two setups and no experiment file and sets `Generated 2 setups (2 new) and 0 experiments.`. `a kit opened read-only generates nothing`: over the folder reopened read-only, the grid sets `kitStatus` to `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.` and every file is as it was. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Acceptance: After `GenerateSetupGrid` lands, the message MUST record every ticked combination's setup not yet held, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of a committable draft over each, refuse an impossible grid and a read-only kit with nothing written, and `AGENTS.md` MUST carry the naming-template gotcha; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each`, `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing`, `a grid over a draft that cannot be committed records its setups and no experiment` and `a kit opened read-only generates nothing`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.",
