n point order), `member this.withoutExclusion (point : MappedPointNumber) : MappedAttachment` (that point's exclusion removed; the attachment unchanged when it has none) and `member this.tryFindExclusion (point : MappedPointNumber) : PointExclusion option`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, after `ExperimentNotes` (step 285): `CorrectionNote of string` with `.value` and `static member tryCreate (text : string) : CorrectionNote option` (`None` for an empty or white-space text); `SetupCorrection = { previous : SetupReference; corrected : SetupReference; note : CorrectionNote }`, one re-pointing of the experiment's setup and why it was made. `Experiment` gains `corrections : SetupCorrection list` after `dataOpt`, oldest first. `commit` (step 290) gives an appended experiment `[]` and keeps an edited one's, so an edit never loses its audit trail. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json` (steps 288, 290, 291), schema version 1 kept (no kit of the old shape exists outside test output, .spec-md \u00a77): a non-null `dataOpt` holds exactly `attachment`, `profile`, `rows` and `exclusions`, an array of objects holding exactly `point` (an integer from 1) and `reason` (a string holding a non-white-space character); `experiment` also holds `corrections`, an array of objects holding exactly `previous` and `corrected` (each the object `experiment.setup` is, step 261) and `note` (a string holding a non-white-space character). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 224, 261, 291, 306) keeps each copied experiment's exclusions and corrections as written; only its id, its name and its attachment's path are given anew, as before. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the `AttachDataFile` arm (step 310) builds its mapped attachment with `exclusions = []`; nothing else in the window changes. (6) Every fixture that builds a `MappedAttachment` sets `exclusions = []`, and every fixture that buil