      "requirement": "Step 361: A study opens a material version into a working copy whose every component is a parameter, generated from the material's crystal record, shared by every sample made of it (001 \u00a7I 'Material parameters as unknowns: a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file, with `Unknown` components; every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; 001 \u00a7N 'Parameter-axis generation: \u2026 publishes its `ParameterAxis` list. Case 1b's generated axes equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` \u2014 an exact test'; 001 \u00a7P `OpenMaterial`; the S11.1 brief 'Generated axes', 'the EXACT test'; .spec-md \u00a73.16 'its generated axes are that record's `axes`'). A complexity tree publishes no parameter axis in this spec: its eps is formula, table or constant data the ladder edits, so a material is fitted through its crystal-parameter form (step 355). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 360's member: (1) `type ParameterAxis<'Parameters> with member this.parameterValueOf (p : 'Parameters) : ParameterValue` (`this.read p` as a `ParameterValue`, the one conversion from an axis read to a parameter's number) and `member this.writeValue (value : ParameterValue) (p : 'Parameters) : 'Parameters` (`this.write value.value p`, the one conversion back). (2) `type CrystalParameters with member this.parameterAxes : ParameterAxis<CrystalParameters> list`: the axes of its record (`UniaxialParameters.axes`, `TriclinicParameters.axes` or `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, step 353) in their order, each lifted onto the crystal by a private helper per case: the same `name` and the same field case (`RefractionIndexField`, `RhoValueField`, `EpsValueField`), its access reading the record of a crystal of the same case and writing back a crystal of that case; a crystal of another case reads as `this` reads and is written back unchanged, because the axes are ge