      "requirement": "Step 362: The study's unknowns, each with its scope, and the owners each scope gives it (001 \u00a7L 'the unknowns (owner + scope)' and the scope table: ItemScope 'One value for every experiment using the item', MaterialScope 'One value for every sample of an opened material', SessionScope 'One value per session block (gain)', ExperimentScope 'One value per run'; 001 \u00a7I 'Intensity detector | Gain (session-scoped)'; the S11.1 brief 'each with an owner (item / material / session / experiment) and a scope'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 361's members: (1) `UnknownOwner` = `ItemOwner of ItemId` | `MaterialOwner of MaterialVersionId` | `SessionOwner of SessionName` | `ExperimentOwner of ExperimentName`: what holds one value of an unknown; it is derived and never stored, so it carries no tag. (2) `StudyUnknown = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; scope : ParameterScope; unknown : UnknownParameterData }` (step 214's start, bounds and prior). (3) `type Study with member this.scopeOf (parameter : StudyParameterRef) : ParameterScope`: the study's `ScopedParameter` for it, or the default: `MaterialScope` for a material component, `SessionBlockScope` for an item parameter named `gain` (the one `IntensityDetectorModel` publishes, step 208), `ItemScope` for every other item parameter. (4) `member this.unknownsWith (used : Item list) : StudyUnknown list`: for each item of `used` in order, each of its parameters whose state is `UnknownParameter`, then for each opened material in order each component whose state is `UnknownParameter`, each with `scopeOf`; a parameter that is a link's follower is left out, because it takes its leader's value (001 \u00a7L). `used` is the items the study's experiments use (`Experiment.itemsUsedBy`, step 261), which the caller passes. (5) `type StudyUnknown with member this.owners (sessions : StudySession list) (users : ExperimentName list) : UnknownOwner list`: under `ItemScope` or `MaterialScope` its one owner, the `ItemOwner` of its item or the `MaterialOwner` of its material; under `SessionBlockScope` one `SessionOwner` per session holding a user, in session order; under `ExperimentScope` one `ExperimentOwner` per user, in order. `users` is the enabled experiments of the study whose setups use the unknown's item or a sample made of its material, which the forward model knows (S11.2). The fitter's vector holds one value per owner of each unknown (S11.2-S11.3). No other type or member is added. Tests, in `StudyTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216) over the built-in circular-polarizer and intensity-detector models: CPL1 with `c2.retardance` unknown, CPL2 with `c2.retardance` and `c2.fastAxisOffset` unknown, a Phone with `gain` unknown, and an opened absorbing material with `n1` and `e11` unknown: `the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers`: `unknownsWith [ CPL1; CPL2; Phone ]` answers CPL1 `c2.retardance` (ItemScope), CPL2's two (ItemScope), Phone `gain` (SessionBlockScope), `n1` and `e11` (MaterialScope), in that order; with a `ScopedParameter` making CPL1's `ExperimentScope` it answers that scope; with a link (a record literal) whose follower is CPL2's `c2.retardance` that parameter is left out. `an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user`: over sessions `Session 1` [E1; E2] and `Session 2` [E3], CPL1's unknown has the one `ItemOwner`, `n1` the one `MaterialOwner`, Phone's `gain` with users [E1; E3] `SessionOwner` of both sessions and with users [E2] only `Session 1`, and an `ExperimentScope` unknown with users [E3; E1] the owners E3 then E1. Acceptance: After the unknowns land, `Study.unknownsWith` MUST list the used items' and opened materials' unknown parameters with their scopes (a detector's `gain` session-scoped by default) and leave out link followers, and `StudyUnknown.own