      "id": "S115-FIT-PROVENANCE",
      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7L ('Publishing: item \u2192 next revision (Calibrated); material or black-box object \u2192 Promote to library'; 'staged: \u2026 Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with \u03c3'; 'Results, stored in the fit run'), \u00a7I ('Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history; \"Publish calibration\" writes the next revision. Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'; 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance \"fitted in kit K, study S, run R\"'), \u00a7O ('Study view: the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links); Run joint / Run stage; the fit-run history; results tabs: values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood'; the flow strip; 'Automation': StudyRunFitButton, every new control a uniquely named static member of ConstructorUiId), \u00a7R ('SolverHandoffView's stub screen, replaced by the study view. Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'), \u00a7P (CreateStudy, AddExperimentsToStudy, OpenMaterial, SetParameterScope, LinkParameters, RunFit, PublishCalibration, PromoteToLibrary; the same messages back the buttons), \u00a7N ('Long fits run on JobRunner, with progress and cancel; the fit run is written on completion'); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 40 (S11.5) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.22, \u00a74, \u00a75, \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79, \u00a710; AGENTS.md (elevate every primitive, unique names, errors are values, reuse never copy, no legacy, comments)",
      "requirement": "Step 405: A promoted library entry says where it was fitted (001 \u00a7I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance \"fitted in kit K, study S, run R\"'; 001 \u00a7L 'Publishing: \u2026 material or black-box object \u2192 Promote to library'; the S11.5 brief 'add an EntryProvenance case here if none fits'). None fits: `UserProvenance` carries nothing and `KitImportProvenance` names the kit alone (`LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, steps 24, 91). The study and the fit run are named by the file stems the kit stores them under (001 \u00a7A), because `StudyName` and `FitRunName` are declared after this file (steps 214, 358) and their `fileStem` members (steps 358, 383) are how a kit names them; nothing is moved. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `EntryProvenance` (steps 24, 91) gains a sixth case, `FitProvenance of EntryFitInfo`, declared together with `and EntryFitInfo = { kit : KitId; studyStem : FileStem; fitRunStem : FileStem }`: the kit the fit ran in (step 24's `KitId`) and the stems of the study's `<study>.study-json` and of the fit run's `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`, the files that reproduce the fitted values (001 \u00a7I 'Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'). A fitted entry belongs to the user: `protection` answers `UserManaged`, `categoryOrigin` answers `UserCategory`, and `attributionOpt` (step 113) answers `None`, because a fit carries no licence. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (steps 63, 91): `kindValue` answers 6 for a fit and `catalogueIdOpt` answers `None`, because a fitted entry ships in no catalogue. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (steps 30, 91): the provenance definition gains a sixth shape, exactly what the serializer writes for `FitProvenance`: `kit` a GUID, and `studyStem` and `fitRunStem` non-empty strings. The ent