    {
      "id": "S115-CALIBRATION",
      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7L ('Publishing: item \u2192 next revision (Calibrated); material or black-box object \u2192 Promote to library'; 'staged: \u2026 Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with \u03c3'; 'Results, stored in the fit run'), \u00a7I ('Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history; \"Publish calibration\" writes the next revision. Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'; 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance \"fitted in kit K, study S, run R\"'), \u00a7O ('Study view: the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links); Run joint / Run stage; the fit-run history; results tabs: values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood'; the flow strip; 'Automation': StudyRunFitButton, every new control a uniquely named static member of ConstructorUiId), \u00a7R ('SolverHandoffView's stub screen, replaced by the study view. Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'), \u00a7P (CreateStudy, AddExperimentsToStudy, OpenMaterial, SetParameterScope, LinkParameters, RunFit, PublishCalibration, PromoteToLibrary; the same messages back the buttons), \u00a7N ('Long fits run on JobRunner, with progress and cancel; the fit run is written on completion'); specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 40 (S11.5) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.22, \u00a74, \u00a75, \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79, \u00a710; AGENTS.md (elevate every primitive, unique names, errors are values, reuse never copy, no legacy, comments)",
      "requirement": "Step 406: Publish calibration, as a pure update of the kit's items: a fit run's item-owned values become the items' next revisions, each value a `CalibratedParameter` with its \u03c3 and its fit run (001 \u00a7I 'Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history; \"Publish calibration\" writes the next revision. Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'; 001 \u00a7L 'Publishing: item \u2192 next revision (`Calibrated`)', 'staged: stage 1 calibrates items \u2026; Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with \u03c3', 'Explicit links (\"CPL2.\u03b4 = CPL1.\u03b4\") are constraints'; 001 \u00a7P `PublishCalibration`; the S11.5 brief). It REUSES `Item.publishRevision` (step 235), the one revision write, and reads the \u03c3 S11.4 stores (`FitRunResults.sigmas`, steps 396, 404); recording the items is the window's (step 413). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5, and every case name has two words. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs`, `module StudyPublishing` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `FitRuns.fs` (step 383), the last Domain file, because publishing reads studies, items, fit runs and the kit's library: one `<Compile Include=\"StudyPublishing.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: what a fit run publishes back into the kit and the library (spec 0050 S11.5). In order: (1) `PublishError`, an `*Error` union: `ForeignFitRunErr of reason : string` (the fit run is another study's), `UnknownPublishedItemErr of reason : string` (the run fitted an item the kit no longer holds), `UndeterminedSigmaErr of reason : string` (a fitted value whose \u03c3 the run leaves undetermined, step 396's `sigmaOpt = None`), `NoCalibrationErr of reason : string` (the run fitted no item-owned value), `CalibrationAlreadyPublishedErr of reason : string` (every item already holds the run's calibration) and `PublishItemErr of error : ItemError` (step 213), with `member this.describe : string`: `the fit run belongs to another study: <reason>`, `the kit has no such item: <reason>`, `the fit leaves a sigma undetermined: <reason>`, `the fit run calibrates no item: <reason>`, `the calibration is already published: <reason>` and `the item refused the calibration: <the error's describe>`. (2) `type Study with member this.calibratedItemsWith (run : FitRun) (items : Item list) : Result<Item list, PublishError>`, over the kit's items, in this order. `run.study` other than `this.name` is `ForeignFitRunErr` naming both. The item-owned entries are the `run.entries` (step 383) whose `parameter` is `ItemParameterRef (id, name)` and whose `owner` is `ItemOwner id`, in entry order; one whose item `items` lacks is `UnknownPublishedItemErr` naming its GUID and the run. Each one's \u03c3 is the `sigmaOpt` of the `run.results.sigmas` element whose `entry` is `{ parameter = e.parameter; owner = e.owner }` (`FitEntryRef`, step 396); `None`, or no element, is `UndeterminedSigmaErr` naming the item's label, the parameter and the run. No item-owned entry is `NoCalibrationErr` naming the run. An entry owned by a session or an experiment (`SessionOwner`, `ExperimentOwner`, step 362) holds one value per session block or run and is no item's calibration, so it is left out and stays in the fit run (001 \u00a7L scope table). Each item-owned entry publishes `{ name = name; state = CalibratedParameter { value = e.fitted; sigma = <its \u03c3>; fitRun = run.name } }` (step 214). Each `this.links` link (step 364) whose leader is a published `ItemParameterRef` and whose follower is an `ItemParameterRef` of an item of `items` publishes the leader's state under the follower's name, so stage 2 finds the follower calibrated as `stageWith` requires (step 385, `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr`). Per item of `items`, in order, its published parameters are its own entries in entry order, then its followers in link order; one whose state the item already holds is dropped, and an item with none left is not published, so publishing one run twice writes no second revision. None left at all is `CalibrationAlreadyPublishedErr` naming the run. Each remaining item is `item.publishRevision <its published parameters>` (step 235), an `ItemError` answering `PublishItemErr`. The answer is the published items, in `items` order. Nothing is written and no clock is read. No other type or member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs`, `module StudyPublishingTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216) as `StudyTests` makes them (step 362): CPL1 and CPL2 over the built-in circular-polarizer model, each with `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2], and a Phone over the intensity-detector model with `gain` unknown from 1000 within [100, 10000]; a test-local study record `QZ-LR` whose one link makes CPL2's `c2.retardance` follow CPL1's; and a test-local `FitRun` record (steps 383, 404) of `QZ-LR` named `FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\"`, whose entries are CPL1's `c2.retardance` (`ItemOwner`) fitted at 1.55 and the Phone's `gain` (`SessionOwner (SessionName \"Session 1\")`) fitted at 900, and whose results hold CPL1's \u03c3 `Some (ParameterSigma 0.002)`, the gain's `None` and five empty lists. `publishing a calibration writes each item-owned fitted value with its sigma and fit run into the item's next revision, and a linked follower takes its leader's`: `calibratedItemsWith run [ CPL1; CPL2; Phone ]` answers CPL1 then CPL2, each at revision 2 whose history is the one record of revision 1's values and whose `c2.retardance` is `CalibratedParameter { value = 1.55; sigma = ParameterSigma 0.002; fitRun = FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\" }`, every other parameter