shingTests` (step 406). `a promoted material is its opened version's entry with the crystal its fit run produced`: over a test-local absorbing crystal entry of fifteen distinct literal values (as `StudyMaterialTests` builds its probe, step 361) opened by the study, with `n1` and `e11` unknown, and a run of the study fitting `n1` at 1.7 and `e11` at 0.02 (`MaterialOwner`) whose `parameters` record every other component at the probe's value: `promotedMaterialWith` answers the entry under `CrystalParameterPhysics` whose generated axes read 1.7 for `n1`, 0.02 for `e11` and the probe's value for every other component, its id and name unchanged. `a material component fitted per run, or a material the study did not open or the run did not fit, is not promoted`: `n1` owned by an `ExperimentOwner` answers `ScopedPromotionErr` naming `n1`; a version the study did not open, and a run with no entry of the material, each answer `UnfittedPromotionErr`. `a promoted black box is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix under the item's GUID and label`: QZ over the built-in black-box model (`ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId`, sixteen elements at the identity, step 208), with `m00` fitted at 0.9 and `m01` at 0.25 (`ItemOwner`), answers the preset whose id is QZ's GUID text, named `QZ`, `CustomMueller` and `UserManaged`, with one `ConstantMueller` component at offset zero whose matrix holds 0.9 at (0, 0), 0.25 at (0, 1) and the identity elsewhere, within 1e-15; CPL1 over the circular-polarizer model answers `NotBlackBoxErr` naming `CPL1`; and QZ's `m01` owned by an `ExperimentOwner` answers `ScopedPromotionErr`. `a fit run's provenance names its kit, its study's file and its own file`: `provenanceIn` of a test-local `KitId` is `FitProvenance { kit = <it>; studyStem = FileStem \"QZ-LR\"; fitRunStem = FileStem \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\" }`. `a fit run offers each opened material and black box it fitted for promotion`: over CPL1, QZ and the opened material, `promotionSub