      "requirement": "Step 428: The reference kit is committed as AT-1's build writes it, once, and never by hand (001 \u00a7Q 'Section 12 creates them by running the build below once, through the app's own folder `KitProxy`, and commits the result. They are never hand-written'; 001 \u00a71 'complete kit folders \u2026 `library/` and the raw lab files under `data/`'; .spec-md \u00a73.13). (1) The fact `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` in `KitAcceptanceTests`: it builds the kit (`buildOpticsMuellerKit`, steps 421-427) into a fresh run folder and compares it with the committed kit (`CommittedKit.OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, .spec-md \u00a73.21): the two folders' relative file paths, `.oc/` left out of both, are the same set, and each file's bytes are equal: every kit file at the root, every file under `library/` and every file under `data/` (001 \u00a7Q 'every kit file and every file under `data/` and `library/`; `.oc/` excluded'). A difference fails naming the built folder's absolute path, the first differing relative path and why (missing, extra or different bytes). It reads the committed kit and writes nothing there (.spec-md \u00a74 'Tests' data'). (2) The committed kit, created by this step once: run the fact (`kit-acceptance`, filtered to it); it fails, because `data/optics-mueller/` holds the lab files alone (step 330), and names its built folder; copy every file of that folder except those under `data/` (the committed lab files, equal by the step-421 fact) and under `.oc/` into `data/optics-mueller/`, keeping their relative paths and bytes; run the fact again, and it passes. The files are the kit file, the nine `<label>.item-json`, the forty-two `<setup>.setup-json`, the fifty-three `<experiment>.experiment-json`, `QZ-LR.study-json`, the two `QZ-LR@<stamp>.fitrun-json` and `library/`'s snapshots of the built-in entries the kit references, each `library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json` named by a GUID the built-in catalogue froze (s