      "requirement": "Step 432: AT-2 starts its kit (001 \u00a71b; 001 \u00a7Q 'Common rules' 'Build: each test builds its kit ONLY through the semantic messages (\u00a7P), against a SQLite `:memory:` library, and writes it through the REAL folder `KitProxy` into a throw-away folder under the test run's output directory'; 001 \u00a7Q AT-2 'Kit: a source at `referenceWaveLength`; an ideal polarimeter detector with the `NoiseParam.decentLab` noise model; five sample items \u2014 100 \u00b5m plates cut \u2026 \u2014 all made of ONE material version holding the `absorbing` ground truth'). A crystal material reaches the library through its entry file (step 355), so the build drops the material and its plate sample on the Library window, as a user drops files they were given (001 \u00a7H; steps 104, 111). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs` (step 421), each private function documented in one line citing spec 0050 S12.2: (1) Shared with AT-1, so one composition exists (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'): the test clock and the start screen `buildOpticsMuellerKit` composes inline (step 421 (c), (d)) become `testClockAt (instant : ClockTime)`, answering a `ClockProvider` over a mutable cell and that cell, which only a build sets to move its clock, and `kitStartOver (context : AppContext) (clock : ClockProvider) (kitId : KitId) (author : KitAuthor) (folder : KitFolder)`, the `KitStartModel` and the cell its `showKit` keeps the opened kit in; `buildOpticsMuellerKit` calls them with its own values, and every AT-1 fact keeps its assertions. (2) `buildAbsorbingKit (run : FolderName)`, which later steps extend, answers the built folder, the app context, the window model and the test clock, in this order. (a) The folder is `<System.AppContext.BaseDirectory>/KitAcceptanceTests/<run>/absorbing-biaxial-noisy`, created fresh and empty, its leaf naming the kit (step 145). (b) The context is `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitAcceptanceTests\")` (steps 83, 100)