      "requirement": "Step 472: The kit's looks, and the structural report over them: 'this kit can never recover X' and 'you need an off-axis cut' for a real kit (001 \u00a7M 'It answers outright \"this kit can never recover X\" and \"you need an off-axis cut\"'; the S14.1 brief). The kit holds no angle limit, because no item model publishes one (step 208), so its angle range is the table's: any plate tilts from normal incidence to `IncidenceAngle.maxValue` (`Fields.fs:30`), and those two incidences bound everything layer 1 can tell of a tilt. In `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, on `PlannerInputs` (step 471), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.1: (1) `member this.looks : PlannerLook list`: for each plate in order, each reach of `this.lab.reaches` in order (step 470), each incidence of `[ IncidenceAngle.normal; IncidenceAngle.maxValue ]` and each observable the plate's emission allows (`EmitBoth` transmitted then reflected, `EmitTransmittedOnly` transmitted, `EmitReflectedOnly` reflected, `Placement.fs:Emission`, matched by case), the look `{ normalAxisOpt = plate.normalAxisOpt; incidence; observable; reach }`. (2) `member this.structuralReport : Result<RecoverabilityReport, PlannerError>`: `this.prior.crystal.structuralReport this.targets this.looks` (step 469). No other member is added; the numerical layer, the plan and its cache are S14.2's. Tests, in `PlannerInputsTests`, over step 471's kit (its uniaxial version, plates QZ-Z and QZ-X, and items from step 470), each study freeing all four components so the targets are n_o, n_e, g11 and g33: `a kit's looks are each plate under each reach, at normal and steepest incidence, on each branch its emission allows`: with plates QZ-Z (`EmitBoth`) and QZ-X (`EmitTransmittedOnly`) and the Polarimeter and Ellipsometer, `looks` holds twelve looks in the order above: QZ-Z's eight (full Mueller, then ellipsometric; normal, then 89 degrees; transmitted, then reflected) on `ThirdCrystalAxis`, then QZ-X's four, transmitted only, on `FirstCrystalAxis`. `a kit of z-cut plates needs an off-axis cut, and one without a full Mueller reach never recovers the gyration`: with QZ-Z and the Polarimeter, the report has every target reachable and one finding, `OffAxisCutFinding { targets = [ n_e; g33 ]; capAngle = <the crystal's snellCap>; cuts = [ XCut ] }`: a tilt reaches n_e and g33, at most the cap off the normal; adding QZ-X removes it; with QZ-Z, QZ-X, Phone and LP1 (a single polarizer), g11 and g33 are `UnrecoverableTargetFinding`s of `FullMuellerNeededReason` with `[ FullMuellerRemedy ]` while n_o and n_e are reachable. `a kit with no plate of the material can never recover any target`: with the Polarimeter and no plate of the material (GL only), every target's finding is `NoLookReason`, its remedies ending in `FullMuellerRemedy` after at least one `AddPlateRemedy`, and there is no off-axis finding. Acceptance: After the kit report lands, `PlannerInputs.looks` MUST be every plate under every reach at normal and steepest incidence on every branch its emission allows, and `PlannerInputs.structuralReport` MUST report the kit's unrecoverable targets and its need of an off-axis cut; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's looks are each plate under each reach, at normal and steepest incidence, on each branch its emission allows`, `a kit of z-cut plates needs an off-axis cut, and one without a full Mueller reach never recovers the gyration` and `a kit with no plate of the material can never recover any target`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.",
