      "requirement": "Step 477: The Measurement Planner's layer-2 core: the Fisher information of a set of candidate experiments, its rank, its confounded combinations and the Cram\u00e9r\u2013Rao bound per target (001 \u00a7M 'Layer 2, numerical (local, at a nominal point): the Fisher information from the Jacobians of every candidate experiment \u2026; rank (identifiable combinations); smallest singular vectors (confounded combinations, e.g. thickness \u2194 n); Cram\u00e9r\u2013Rao bounds per target'; the S14.2 brief). It REUSES `ResidualJacobian` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualJacobian`: its `rank`, step 394, and `conditionNumber`), `FitQuality.covarianceOf` (step 476) and `FitUncertainty.ParameterWeights` (step 342); no second inverse, rank floor or condition number is written. The information of candidates whose rows J_i carry noise variances \u03c3_i\u00b2 is F = \u03a3 J_i\u1d40 J_i / \u03c3_i\u00b2, and the bound per target is \u221adiag(F\u207b\u00b9). The rows are kept scaled to one reference noise, the first candidate's, so the bound is `covarianceOf` of those rows with that noise as its reduced \u03c7\u00b2: by construction the covariance a fit of those candidates reports when its residual level is their noise, which the promoted `predictedRelativeErrors` reads (step 342). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2; every case name has two words; no `bool` appears. (1) Domain, `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 472's members, because the planner's cache stores them (step 485): `NoiseVariance of float` with `.value`, the variance of one residual entry of a candidate in its residual's units squared; `CandidateRows = { jacobian : ResidualJacobian; noise : NoiseVariance }`, one candidate's information, its residual Jacobian over the targets' scaled coordinates and its entries' noise; and `PlannerError` (step 469) gains `NoiselessPlannerCandidateErr` (`the candidate's noise variance is not above zero: <reason>`) and `PlannerShapeErr` (`the candidate's Jacobian does not fit the targets: <reason>`), each `of reason : string` with its `describe` arm. (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/PlannerInformation.fs`, `module PlannerInformation` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`'s compile list (one `<Compile Include=\"PlannerInformation.fs\" />` line, no comment), because it reads `FitQuality`, `FitUncertainty`, `MuellerFitting`, `BenchNoise`, `FittedProblems` (step 476) and `StudyEngine`. Module doc: the Measurement Planner's numerical layer, the Fisher information of candidate experiments at a nominal point (spec 0050 S14.2). In order: (a) `SingularValue of float` with `.value`. (b) `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"the singular values and right singular vectors of a residual Jacobian, read whole from the MathNet SVD\")>] SingularSpectrum = { values : float[]; rightVectors : float[][] }`, with `static member ofRows (rows : float[][]) (coordinateCount : int) : SingularSpectrum`, marked `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof InteropBoundary, \"the MathNet SVD of a residual Jacobian, its right singular vectors read whole\")>]` (AGENTS.md: a call into a third-party numeric library is marked on its own declaration): with no row, `coordinateCount` zeros and the identity's rows; otherwise `Svd(true)` of `RealMatrix.create rows`, reached as `MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber` reaches it, its `S` in MathNet's descending order padded with zeros to `coordinateCount` and the rows of its `VT`. (c) `SingularDirection = { singularValue : SingularValue; weights : ParameterWeights }`, with `member this.text (coordinates : ParameterName list) : string`: each coordinate whose weight is at least a tenth of the largest in magnitude, in coordinate order, written `+<w> <name>` or `-<w> <name>` with two decimals under `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`, joined by single spaces. (d) `InformationLogDeterminant of float` and `CovarianceTrace of float`,