fiable combinations (0 at rank 0); `this.traceOpt : CovarianceTrace option`, the sum of the squares of `scaledSigmasOpt` when it is `Some`; and `this.boundsOver (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) : TargetBound list option` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ParameterScaling`), for `scaledSigmasOpt = Some s` each coordinate k's bound `ParameterSigma (s_k \u00b7 |axis.read scaling.scale|)`, the axis being `scaling.axes`' k-th, the one the rows' coordinate k is scaled by, and `None` otherwise. (g) `type ReducedChiSquared with member this.noiseVariance : NoiseVariance` (`FitQuality.fs:ReducedChiSquared`): the noise variance a fit's reduced \u03c7\u00b2 estimates, the residual level of measured data read as a candidate's noise. No cache, threshold, regularisation or option is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlannerInformationTests.fs`, `module PlannerInformationTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over Jacobians written as literals and test-local coordinate names. `the Cramer-Rao bound is the covariance a fit reports when its residual level is the noise`: over the coordinates of `UniaxialParameters.axes`' first two axes (n_o, n_e), the candidate J = [[1; 0]; [1; 1]; [0; 2]] with noise 0.04 has `scaledSigmasOpt` [0.2 \u00b7 \u221a(5/9); 0.2 \u00b7 \u221a(2/9)] within 1e-12 ((J\u1d40J)\u207b\u00b9 = [[5; \u22121]; [\u22121; 2]] / 9, written out in the test); the same rows as two candidates, the first row at noise 0.04 and the last two doubled at noise 0.16, give the same sigmas within 1e-12; and `boundsOver` a scaling over those two axes whose scale holds 1e-3 for both indices answers those sigmas times 1e-3 under the names n_o and n_e. `two coordinates the candidates move only together are one confounded combination`: over coordinates a, b and c, J = [[1; 1; 0]; [2; 2; 1]] at noise 1 has rank 2, `conditionOpt`, `scaledSigmasOpt` and `boundsOver` `None`, one confounded direction whose weights are \u00b1(1/\u221a2, \u22121/\u221a2, 0) within 1e-12 and whose text is `+0.71 a -0.71 b` or `-0.71 a +0.71 b`, and a weakest direction whose singular value is above zero. `with no candidate nothing is identifiable, and a noiseless or misshapen candidate is refused`: over no candidate the rank is 0, the three confounded directions are the identity's and `logDeterminant` is 0; a candidate at noise 0 answers `NoiselessPlannerCandidateErr` naming candidate 1, and one of two columns over three coordinates `PlannerShapeErr` naming both counts, each `describe` starting with its rendered prefix. `the log determinant counts each identifiable combination, and the trace sums the targets' variances`: J = [[2; 0]; [0; 3]] at noise 1 has `logDeterminant` 2 ln 2 + 2 ln 3 and `traceOpt` 1/4 + 1/9, and at noise 4 `logDeterminant` 2 ln 2 + 2 ln 3 \u2212 2 ln 4, each within 1e-12; and `(ReducedChiSquared 0.25).noiseVariance` is `NoiseVariance 0.25`. Acceptance: After the core lands, `PlannerInformation.over` MUST stack each candidate's rows scaled to the reference noise and answer its rank, confounded and weakest combinations, condition, log determinant, trace and Cram\u00e9r\u2013Rao sigmas as `FitQuality.covarianceOf` gives them, refusing a noiseless or misshapen candidate; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the Cramer-Rao bound is the covariance a fit reports when its residual level is the noise`, `two coordinates the candidates move only together are one confounded combination`, `with no candidate nothing is identifiable, and a noiseless or misshapen candidate is refused` and `the log determinant counts each identifiable combination, and the trace sums the targets' variances`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.",
