      "source": "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md \u00a7M ('Layer 2, numerical (local, at a nominal point): the Fisher information from the Jacobians of every candidate experiment - the study engine's own forward model and Jacobian, REUSED; rank (identifiable combinations); smallest singular vectors (confounded combinations, e.g. thickness <-> n); Cramer-Rao bounds per target; greedy D-optimal (or target-restricted A-optimal) selection of the next experiment; the instrument-matrix condition number for choosing polarizer and compensator states'; 'Output: a recoverability report; a measurement plan emitted as setups + experiments with role Planned into the same kit'; 'Cache: key = hash of (items + parameter states + targets + nominal point); stored in the kit's .oc/planner/ (derived, safe to delete, never sent); candidate Jacobians are cached per (sample, experiment)'; 'Workflow'; the Full rank and Layer 2 / Cramer-Rao acceptance facts), \u00a7O ('Plan view: the recoverability report (rank, confounded combinations, CRB per target) and the ranked candidates, with Add to kit'; the flow strip's Plan step; PlanRunButton), \u00a7P (RunPlan), \u00a7Q (predictedRelativeErrors and the bench noise model promoted for the Planner), \u00a7W; specs/0050/.section-plan-jsonl section 46 (S14.2) brief; specs/0050/.spec-md \u00a73.12, \u00a73.22, \u00a74, \u00a75, \u00a76, \u00a78, \u00a79, \u00a710; AGENTS.md (elevate every primitive, unique names, errors are values, reuse never copy, comments, UI automation ids)",
      "requirement": "Step 479: A candidate's information from its measurement configurations, through the study engine's own forward model and residual, and its noise from the detector's bench budget (001 \u00a7M 'each detector's noise model (the bench model \u00a7Q promotes)'; 001 \u00a7Q AT-2 'Promoted to product \u2026 because the study engine, the \"simulate measurement\" path and the Planner need them: the bench noise model'; the S14.2 brief). A polarimeter observation of a plate is predicted by the forward the study engine solves it with (`createBerremanForward`, step 375), and its residual entries are `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor`'s (step 336), the study residual's layout (step 379): the fifteen normalized-element entries of every observation, then one log-throughput entry per observation. A budget's numbers are uniform max errors (`NoiseParam`, Optimization/BenchNoise.fs from S10.1 step 339), a half-width u having the variance u\u00b2 / 3, on each normalized element (`element`), on the throughput (`throughput`) and on the incidence and the azimuth of every configuration (`rotation`, the misalignment `BenchNoise.disturb` draws, steps 339 and 476). The planner takes, linearised at the nominal point, the mean over a candidate's entries of each entry's expected squared error: the reduced \u03c7\u00b2 a fit of its noisy data expects. In `PlannerInformation.fs`, after step 478's declarations, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2: (1) `type NoiseParam with member this.noiseVarianceOver (forward : ForwardModelProxy<'Parameters>) (nominal : 'Parameters) (configurations : MeasurementConfiguration list) : Result<NoiseVariance, MuellerFitError>`. The observations are `MuellerFitting.observeWith forward nominal configurations` (step 335), an error passing through. The angle sensitivity is the two-column `ResidualJacobian` `(ScaledVector [| 0.0; 0.0 |]).offsetJacobianOf` (step 476) of the closure that, for a scaled vector (\u0394i, \u0394a) in radians, files at each nominal configuration c the matrix `forward.muellerOf (c.misalignedBy (Angle \u0394i) (Angle \u0394a)) nominal` (step 476; data filed against the nominal configuration, as `noisyObserveWith` files it) and answers `throughputResidualFor forward <those observations> (MuellerFitting.scalingAround [] nominal nominal)` at `ScaledVector [||]` (a scaling of no axis, whose closure evaluates `nominal`); a forward error inside gives every entry of a residual of that length the 1.0e3 penalty `residualFor` uses (step 336), so the closure is total. For entry i of the 16 \u00b7 m entries of m observations the variance is `this.element.value\u00b2 / 3` for i below 15 \u00b7 m and `this.throughput.value\u00b2 / 3` from there, plus `this.rotation.value\u00b2 / 3 \u00b7 (a_i0\u00b2 + a_i1\u00b2)`, `rotation.value` in radians and a_i the entry's row of the angle sensitivity; the answer is the mean over the entries as a `NoiseVariance`. (2) `candidateRowsOver (forward : ForwardModelProxy<'Parameters>) (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (nominal : 'Parameters) (noise : NoiseParam) (configurations : MeasurementConfiguration list) : Result<CandidateRows, MuellerFitError>`, a generic function of the module: its `jacobian` is `(toScaled scaling nominal).offsetJacobianOf (throughputResidualFor forward <observeWith forward nominal configurations> scaling)` (`MuellerInverse.fs:toScaled`), the residual of noiseless observations at the nominal point, whose Jacobian is the study residual's there because the measured readings enter it as constants; its `noise` is `noise.noiseVarianceOver forward nominal configurations`. The offset frame (step 476) takes the derivative about the nominal point however its scaling is centred, a component at zero included. No cache, simulation seed or option is added. Tests, in `PlannerInformationTests`, over a test-local `ForwardModelProxy<UniaxialParameters>` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ForwardModelProxy`) and two configurations built by `MuellerFitting.configurationOf` (`XCut`, 1 mm, incidences 10\u00b0 and 20\u00b0, azimuth 0\u00b0, `TransmittedMueller`, 632.8 nm): `a noise budget's variance is each reading's uniform variance plus the misalignment it turns into reading error`: with a forward answering the identity Mueller matrix with m01 = 0.5 \u00d7 the configuration's incidence in radians (m00 = 1, the parameters ignored), `NoiseParam.noiseless` gives `NoiseVariance 0.0`; a budget of element 0.006 alone gives 15 \u00b7 0.006\u00b2 / 3 / 16, of throughput 0.03 alone 0.03\u00b2 / 3 / 16, and of rotation 0.01 rad alone (0.01\u00b2 / 3) \u00b7 0.5\u00b2 / 16, each within 1e-9 relative. `a candidate's rows are the study residual's Jacobian at the nominal point in its scaling's units`: with a forward whose m01 is 2 \u00b7 n_o and m02 is 0.5 \u00b7 n_e (m00 = 1), over a scaling of `UniaxialParameters.axes`' first two axes whose scale holds 1e-3 for both indices, centred at a nominal crystal of n_o 1.544 and n_e 1.553, `candidateRowsOver` over the first configuration answers 16 rows of two columns whose only non-zero entries are one of magnitude 2e-3 in the n_o column and one of magnitude 0.5e-3 in the n_e column, each within 1e-9 relative, every other entry within 1e-12 of zero; the same at a nominal n_o of 0.0, the component at zero; and its noise the budget's variance over that configuration. Add type ParameterValues with member this.benchNoise : Result<NoiseParam, ItemEvaluationError> in Optimization/BenchNoise.fs. It MUST read the three ParameterName noise members, reject missing, non-finite or negative values (and element/throughput values above one) through the typed evaluation errors, and construct the three promoted uncertainty quantities through named source-type conversions. It MUST ignore unrelated parameter entries. This conversion is from a general parameter map to a numerical budget; no second Domain noise record or reverse conversion is introduced. Extend the variance fact to read a budget through