      "requirement": "Step 483: The instrument-matrix condition number for choosing the polarizer and compensator states (001 \u00a7M 'the instrument-matrix condition number for choosing polarizer and compensator states'; the S14.2 brief). A state generator of the kit's polarizer followed by its compensator turned to \u03b8 makes the Stokes state s(\u03b8) = M_C(\u03b8) \u00b7 M_P(0) \u00b7 (1, 0, 0, 0); the analyzer, the same pair in reverse, reads the row a(\u03b8), row 0 of M_P(0) \u00b7 M_C(\u03b8); a reading at generator angle \u03b8_g and analyzer angle \u03b8_a is the design row `MuellerReconstruction.designRow (s \u03b8_g) (a \u03b8_a)` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:designRow`, the row the linear engine solves, step 388), so the instrument matrix of four generator and four analyzer states is the 16 \u00d7 16 stack of those rows, and its condition number (`MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber`) is how much it amplifies reading noise into the reconstructed Mueller matrix. The four angles are the set, from the grid 0\u00b0, 15\u00b0, \u2026, 165\u00b0, whose 4 \u00d7 4 generator matrix has the least condition number (a regular tetrahedron on the Poincar\u00e9 sphere reaches \u221a3), the analyzer turned to the same four; the grid is a constant of the planner. Each optic is evaluated by the one item evaluator (`ItemModelChoice.boundWith`, step 251, at `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters`, step 245; `BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt` at `ElementOrientation.transmittingAt \u03b8`, step 247) at the first source's wavelength. A compound optic (a circular polarizer, step 210) turns as one piece, so it generates states of one ellipticity and cannot complete a basis; it is not paired. In `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 482's declarations. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2; every case name has two words; no `bool` appears. (1) `PlannerError` gains `InstrumentEvaluationErr` (`an optic of the kit cannot be evaluated: <reason>`). (2) `InstrumentChoice = { polarizer : PlannerOptic; compensator : PlannerOptic; angles : Angle list; condition : ConditionNumber }`. (3) `InstrumentFinding` = `ConditionedInstrumentFinding of InstrumentChoice` | `CompensatorMissingFinding of PlannerOptic`, with `member this.text : string`: `<the polarizer's label> with <the compensator's label> at <the four angles in degrees, one decimal, joined by \", \">\u00b0: the instrument matrix's condition number is <\u03ba, two decimals>.` and `<the polarizer's label> has no compensator to pair: it generates linear states only, so a full Mueller matrix needs a retarder.`, under `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`. (4) `type PlannerInputs with member this.instrumentFindingsWith (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) (materials : MaterialProxy) : Result<InstrumentFinding list, PlannerError>`: none without a source; otherwise, for each `PolarizerOptic` of `this.lab.optics` in order, one `ConditionedInstrumentFinding` per `CompensatorOptic` in order \u2014 the four grid angles of least generator condition, a tie keeping the earliest set in the grid's lexicographic order, and the condition of the instrument matrix built over them \u2014 or, when the lab holds no compensator, one `CompensatorMissingFinding` of it. An optic's item missing from `items`, a `choiceOf` answering `None` or an `ItemEvaluationError` answers `InstrumentEvaluationErr` naming the item's label and the cause. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `PlannerInputsTests`, over step 470's items (LP1 the linear-polarizer preset, RET the retarder plate at its quarter-wave default, step 208): `a polarizer and a retarder give the four compensator angles of least generator condition, and the instrument's condition follows`: with Laser, LP1 and RET the answer is one `ConditionedInstrumentFinding` of LP1 with RET whose four angles are distinct grid angles at which the generator matrix's condition, computed in the test through the same evaluator and `conditionNumber`, is no greater than at any other four of the grid's twelve angles (all 495 sets checked), and whose instrument condition is finite and at least 3 (a Kronecker product's condition is its factors' product, each at least \u221a3); its text names both labels and the four angles. `a polarizer alone is told it needs a compensator, and a compound optic is not paired`: with Laser and LP1, or Laser, LP1 and CPL1, the answer is `[ CompensatorMissingFinding LP1 ]` with its text; with no source it is empty. `an optic the library does not resolve refuses the instrument findings, naming it`: a `choiceOf` answering `None` for RET answers `InstrumentEvaluationErr` naming `RET`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Acceptance: After the instrument findings land, `PlannerInputs.instrumentFindingsWith` MUST pair each polarizer with each compensator at the four grid angles of least generator condition and report the instrument matrix's condition, tell a polarizer with no compensator that it needs one, leave compound optics unpaired and refuse an unresolved optic; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a polarizer and a retarder give the four compensator angles of least generator condition, and the instrument's condition follows`, `a polarizer alone is told it needs a compensator, and a compound optic is not paired` and `an optic the library does not resolve refuses the instrument findings, naming it`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.",
