      "requirement": "Step 485: Candidate Jacobians are cached per (sample, experiment) under a key hashing what they depend on (001 \u00a7M 'Cache: key = hash of (items + parameter states + targets + nominal point); stored in the kit's `.oc/planner/` (derived, safe to delete, never sent); candidate Jacobians are cached per (sample, experiment), so adding one item computes only the new candidates'; the S14.2 brief). One candidate's key holds its own items with their parameter states (the source, the plate and the polarimeter: `Item`, step 213, whose `parameters` carry their states), its branch, the opened material (`OpenedMaterial`, steps 361 and 460, whose physics and parameter states are the nominal point and the targets' bounds) and the targets; an item no candidate reads is in no key, so adding one leaves every other key and its entry unchanged, which is how adding one item computes only the new candidates. The file is named by the key's hash and the entry keeps its key, so a stale or colliding file is a miss. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 483's declarations: `PlannerError` gains `PlannerCacheErr` (`the planner's cache cannot be read or written: <reason>`); `PlannerCacheKey = { source : Item; plate : Item; detector : Item; observable : Observable; material : OpenedMaterial; targets : ParameterName list }`; `PlannerCacheEntry = { key : PlannerCacheKey; rows : CandidateRows }` (step 477); and `type PlannerInputs with member this.cacheKeyWith (items : Item list) (candidate : PlanCandidate) : Result<PlannerCacheKey, PlannerError>`: the items of `items` whose ids are the candidate's source's, its plate's and `this.polarimeterOpt`'s detector's (an id `items` lacks, or no polarimeter, answering `UnresolvedPlannerItemErr` naming it), the candidate's observable, `this.prior.material` and `this.targets`. (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/PlannerCacheStore.fs`, `module PlannerCacheStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `KitContentFiles.fs` (one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, no comment). Module doc: the Planner's candidate cache under a kit's `.oc/planner/` (spec 0050 S14.2). It reuses step 124's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.options`) and the content hash (`CanonicalJson.contentHashOf`, step 123); no schema covers the file, because `.oc/` is cache (the lock's rule, step 129). (a) `type PlannerCacheKey with member this.cacheFileName : Result<FileName, StorageError>`: the text of `contentHashOf` of `nodeOf this` (a lower-case hexadecimal SHA-256, step 24) followed by `.candidate-json`. (b) `type PlannerCacheEntry with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf` rendered by `canonicalFileText`) and `type KitFileText with member this.parsePlannerCacheEntry : Result<PlannerCacheEntry, StorageError>`, bound through `CanonicalJson.options` (`MalformedJsonErr`), the lock's pair (step 129). (c) `type KitContext with member this.cachedPlannerRows (key : PlannerCacheKey) (compute : unit -> Result<CandidateRows, PlannerError>) : Result<CandidateRows, PlannerError>`: `this.proxy.readPlannerCacheFile` (step 484) of the key's file name; a text binding to an entry whose `key` equals `key` is a hit, answered without calling `compute`; no file, a text that does not bind and an entry of another key are a miss: `compute ()`, whose `Ok rows` is, under `ReadWriteKitAccess`, written as `{ key; rows }` through `writePlannerCacheFile`, and under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` written nowhere (.spec-md \u00a73.12). A `KitError` or `StorageError` of the read or the write answers `PlannerCacheErr` with its `describe`; a `compute` error passes through and nothing is written. No eviction, size limit, retry or option is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlannerCacheTests.fs`, `module PlannerCacheTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over keys built by `cacheKeyWith` from `PlannerInputsTests`' kit (step 482: Laser, Polarimeter, QZ-Z and its opened material, targets n_e and g33), rows written as literals and a `compute` that counts its calls; the contexts are `KitContext.openKit` (step 131) of `KitProxy.createInMemory` over one initialised `InMemoryKitFolder` unless named otherwise. `a cache miss computes once and writes one file under .oc/planner, and a hit reads it back without computing`: the first call computes once and leaves exactly one `.oc/planner/<64 hex>.candidate-json` in `paths`; a second call with the same key answers rows equal to the first and computes nothing. `a changed item or target is a new key, and an item no candidate reads leaves every key unchanged`: QZ-Z with its `substrateThickness` state changed, or the targets [g33] alone, give another file name; adding an item LP1 to the items leaves `cacheKeyWith` of every candidate equal. `a read-only kit computes and writes nothing, and reads what a read-write open cached`: a read-only context over the folder a read-write one cached reads the hit without computing, and on a miss computes and leaves `paths` unchanged. `a cache file that does not bind, or holds another key, is a miss that is written over`: a file placed at the key's path holding `{`, or the entry of another key, makes the call compute and replace it with the entry of this key. `a folder kit keeps the planner's cache across opens`: over `KitProxy.create` of a folder under the test output, an entry written through a read-write context is read, after that context is closed, through a read-only one without computing. Acceptance: After the cache lands, `PlannerInputs.cacheKeyWith` MUST key a candidate by its own items, branch, opened material and targets, and `KitContext.cachedPlannerRows` MUST answer a hit from `.oc/planner/<hash>.candidate-json` without computing, compute a miss and write it under r